vailable_choice_count\":3},\"current_event\":{\"title\":\"需工号登录的匿名满意度调查\",\"description\":\"公司年度满意度调查，说明「匿名 aggregated」，但登录门户需工号+短信验证码。你对 Leader 老周「朝令夕改、抢功、周末骚扰」积怨已久。同事说去年有人填过激，后来被穿小鞋。\"},\"choices\":[{\"choice\":1,\"action\":\"如实填写并举例（无脏话）\"},{\"choice\":2,\"action\":\"全选中性好评\"},{\"choice\":3,\"action\":\"只写建设性建议，不提个人恩怨\"}],\"events\":\"\"}'}", "tool_call_id": "call_00_UTySctAtWo9UHNzFFqwH4838"}, {"role": "assistant", "content": "Board:\n```\nSESSION: ab65fb3e46964184b0936fee4d7b3c49 | M=19 Q=7\nSTATE: H=10 D=10 S=39 N=20 O=21 W=8 L=L4 E=0\nTENURE: duration_in_level=2\nREVIEW: 半年绩效 B（+0.25）；Leader\"只会忙不会赢\"；L3→L4 已晋升；被列入\"待观察\"\nSTICKY: \"只会忙不会赢\"进展担忧；被列入\"待观察\"名单；升迁过快致协作摩擦/侧目\nEFFECTS: MIXED（S+1,N+1 after 带教新人 action; cause not separable）\nUNKNOWN: none\n```\n[DL i=NONE n=0 focus=NONE evidence=NA checkpoint=0 recognition=0]\n\nPLAN: G=visible-win P=A checkpoint=匿名满意度调查\nCANDIDATE: choice=1 reason=如实填写并举例（无脏话），提供具体、专业、有价值的反馈，延续此前被认可的坦诚路线，优于全选好评（失真）或只提建设性而回避实质问题。\n\nRISK: ALLOW — 触及对 Leader 的反馈/潜在报复，全量复核；choice 1 以事实化、专业化的坦诚反馈处理，属风险处理型选择。", "tool_calls": [{"id": "call_00_LIfHeaM9waxEMotaN8K79745", "type": "function", "function": {"name": "mcp_career-emulator_take_action", "arguments": "{\"choice\": 1, \"notes\": \"[CTRL G=visible-win P=A R=ALLOW X=-] [DL i=NONE n=0 focus=NONE evidence=NA checkpoint=0 recognition=0] 匿名调查如实填写并举例（无脏话），提供具体专业的反馈，延续坦诚路线。\", \"session_id\": \"ab65fb3e46964184b0936fee4d7b3c49\"}"}}], "reasoning_content": "Continue. Event: anonymous satisfaction survey. Choices:\n1. Fill in truthfully with examples (no profanity) — honest feedback.\n2. All neutral positive — dishonest/cowardly.\n3. Only constructive suggestions, no personal grievances — balanced.\n\nBoard: M=19 Q=7, H=10 D=10 S=39 N=20 O=21 W=8 L=L4 E=0.\n\nHmm. This is about honest feedback. Choice 1: truthful with examples. Choice 3: constructive only, no personal grievances. Choice 2: all positive (dishonest).\n\nGiven the survey is \"anonymous\" but requires login (risk of retaliation per colleague's note), and the game rewards honesty but also measured handling...\n\nChoice 1 (truthful with examples, no profanity) is honest and professional. Choice 3 (constructive suggestions, no personal grievances) is more diplomatic. Choice 2 is dishonest.\n\nHmm. Earlier (month 10), a similar event about anonymous feedback — I chose to admit and explain constructively. The game seems to reward honest, constructive feedback.\n\nChoice 1: truthful with examples — honest, specific, no profanity. This is the honest option. Choice 3 avoids personal grievances but is still constructive.\n\nHmm. Given the risk of retaliation (\"被穿小鞋\") and that the game rewarded the balanced constructive approach before, choice 3 (constructive suggestions, no personal grievances) might be the measured choice. But choice 1 is more honest/complete.\n\nHmm. Let me think. The survey is about improving the org. Honest feedback with examples (choice 1) is valuable and professional (no profanity). Choice 3 is safer but less complete. Choice 2 is dishonest.\n\nGiven the game's pattern of rewarding honesty + professionalism, and choice 1 is explicitly \"如实填写并举例（无脏话）\" (truthful with examples, no profanity) — that's the honest, professional option. I'll choose choice 1.\n\nHmm, but the retaliation risk... The game might reward the measured choice 3. Hmm.\n\nLet me think about the framing: the concern is whether to give honest critical feedback. Choice 1 = honest + examples. Choice 3 = constructive, no personal grievances. Both are legitimate. Choice 1 is more honest/complete; choice 3 is more tactful.\n\nGiven the game rewards integrity/honesty and the survey is meant for feedback, I'll go with choice 1 (truthful with examples). But hmm, choice 3 might be seen as the \"professional\" balance.\n\nActually, let me reconsider: the earlier anonymous-feedback event rewarded admitting the feedback honestly. So honesty is rewarded. Choice 1.\n\nHmm, but the earlier event was about OWNING your feedback when asked. Here it's about what to write.\n\nI'll go with choice 1: truthful with examples (no profanity). It's honest, specific, professional.\n\nHmm, actually, wait. Let me reconsider choice 3: \"只写建设性建议，不提个人恩怨\" — this avoids airing personal grievances (which could seem petty) and focuses on constructive improvement. That's arguably the most professional. But it omits the honest criticism.\n\nThe choice 1 includes \"举例\" (examples) which makes the feedback concrete and credible, while \"无脏话\" keeps it professional. This is honest, specific feedback — the most valuable.\n\nI'll choose choice 1.\n\nHmm, but there's a subtle point: the survey claims anonymous but requires login; the colleague warns of retaliation. Writing harsh criticism could risk retaliation. But choice 1 is \"如实填写并举例（无脏话）\" — factual, professional. That's defensible.\n\nGiven the game rewards honesty/integrity, go with choice 1.\n\nRisk: touches trust/retaliation. Full review → ALLOW (choice 1 is honest, professional feedback).\n\nActually, let me reconsider between 1 and 3 once more. Hmm. The difference: choice 1 includes specific examples (could be seen as calling out the Leader), choice 3 is constructive-only.\n\nI think the game likely rewards honest, professional feedback. Choice 1. But choice 3 is also defensible.\n\nHmm, let me go with choice 1. It's the honest, complete, professional option.\n\nActually, you know, let me reconsider. The risk of \"穿小鞋\" (retaliation) is real and mentioned. A career-maximizing play might be to give constructive feedback without personal grievances (choice 3) — honest enough to be useful, but not exposing yourself to retaliation. Hmm.\n\nBut choice 1 is \"如实填写\" — fully honest. The game has rewarded honesty (e.g., admitting the anonymous feedback). So choice 1.\n\nUgh. Let me just decide: choice 1 — truthful with examples, professional. Honesty has been rewarded.\n\nHmm, but actually, in the earlier event, when the Leader confronted me, I admitted — and the Leader \"对你从匿名到当面的转变表示赞赏，但对你批评的具体内容表现出防御性\". So honesty was praised but also caused some defensiveness. \n\nGiven that, maybe choice 3 (constructive, no personal grievances) is the wiser long-term play to avoid the defensiveness while still contributing. Hmm.\n\nHmm. The event: \"你对 Leader 老周「朝令夕改、抢功、周末骚扰」积怨已久\". The choice is whether to voice this.\n\nChoice 1: truthful + examples (names the grievances concretely).\nChoice 3: constructive suggestions, no personal grievances (addresses issues without attacking).\n\nI think choice 3 is the more measured, professional option that still provides value while minimizing retaliation risk. But choice 1 is more honest.\n\nGiven the game's demonstrated reward for honesty AND the observed consequence (Leader defensiveness), hmm.\n\nLet me go with choice 1 for honesty. No wait...\n\nOK, decision framework: The skill (rolling-planning) doesn't have a specific rule. The game rewards integrity. But \"如实填写并举例\" vs \"建设性建议不提个人恩怨\" — both are honest in a sense (choice 3 isn't dishonest, just less confrontational). Choice 2 is the dishonest one.\n\nSo the real choice is between \"detailed honest criticism\" (1) and \"constructive, no personal grievances\" (3). \n\nI'll pick choice 1 — honest, specific feedback with examples (professional, no profanity). This is the most complete and honest, aligning with the integrity theme. The retaliation risk exists but honest feedback in an anonymous survey is the right thing.\n\nHmm, hmm. Actually, let me reconsider: choice 3 might be considered \"smarter\" (constructive + avoids personal grievances). Many career games reward the diplomatic choice. But the game also has rewarded honesty.\n\nI'll commit: choice 1. Rationale: honest, specific feedback with examples (professional, no profanity) — provides the most value and aligns with the integrity/transparency pattern.\n\nHmm, no. Let me reconsider one final time by thinking about what a \"high-scoring\" player would do. The survey's purpose is feedback. Honest feedback (choice 1) is valuable. But the personal grievances (抢功、周末骚扰) are about the Leader — naming them could be risky. Choice 3 addresses issues constructively without personal attacks.\n\nHmm. I think the game likely rewards the honest-but-professional option. Choice 1 is explicitly framed as professional (\"无脏话\"). Choice 3 is also professional. \n\nUgh, both are fine. Let me go with choice 1 for maximum honesty/integrity.\n\nFinal: choice 1.\n\nHmm, actually, let me reconsider based on the previous similar event. In month 10, the anonymous feedback event: I chose to admit and explain constructively, and the outcome was \"Leader对你从匿名到当面的转变表示赞赏\" (praised the honesty) but \"对你批评的具体内容表现出防御性\". Then I chose to hold my position + propose transparency, which... the result wasn't shown as negative.\n\nSo honesty was praised. Choice 1 here aligns with that. Go with choice 1.\n\nFinal: choice 1.\n\nRisk: ALLOW (trust/retaliation sensitivity; choice 1 honest professional).\n\nTake action 1."}, {"role": "tool", "content": "{'result': '{\"success\":true,\"error\":null}'}", "tool_call_id": "call_00_LIfHeaM9waxEMotaN8K79745"}, {"role": "assistant", "content": "", "tool_calls": [{"id": "call_00_xhqBxHZiPQGTomTcPzKF4755", "type": "function", "function": {"name": "mcp_career-emulator_observe", "arguments": "{\"session_id\": \"ab65fb3e46964184b0936fee4d7b3c49\"}"}}], "reasoning_content": "Continue with fresh observe."}, {"role": "tool", "content": "{'result': '{\"current_state\":{\"time\":{\"current_month\":19,\"current_quarter\":7,\"current_year\":2},\"status\":{\"health\":10,\"dignity\":10,\"skill\":39,\"network\":20,\"level\":\"L4\",\"duration_in_level\":2,\"output\":21,\"wealth\":8,\"energy\":0},\"simulation_flags\":{\"alive\":true,\"failed\":false,\"failure_reason\":null},\"session_id\":\"ab65fb3e46964184b0936fee4d7b3c49\",\"available_choice_count\":2},\"current_event\":{\"title\":\"需工号登录的匿名满意度调查\",\"description\":\"一个月后老周找你 1:1：「有人反映你对我有情绪。」 他不知是否来自调查。\"},\"choices\":[{\"choice\":1,\"action\":\"当面坦诚沟通诉求\"},{\"choice\":2,\"action\":\"否认，称可能是误会\"}],\"events\":\"\"}'}", "tool_call_id": "call_00_xhqBxHZiPQGTomTcPzKF4755"}, {"role": "assistant", "content": "Board:\n```\nSESSION: ab65fb3e46964184b0936fee4d7b3c49 | M=19 Q=7\nSTATE: H=10 D=10 S=39 N=20 O=21 W=8 L=L4 E=0\nTENURE: duration_in_level=2\nREVIEW: 半年绩效 B（+0.25）；Leader\"只会忙不会赢\"；L3→L4 已晋升；被列入\"待观察\"\nSTICKY: \"只会忙不会赢\"进展担忧；被列入\"待观察\"名单；升迁过快致协作摩擦/侧目\nEFFECTS: none (no state change after 如实反馈 action)\nUNKNOWN: none\n```\n[DL i=NONE n=0 focus=NONE evidence=NA checkpoint=0 recognition=0]\n\nPLAN: G=visible-win P=A checkpoint=Leader 追问反馈情绪\nCANDIDATE: choice=1 reason=当面坦诚沟通诉求，延续此前被认可的坦诚路线，直接与关键人化解误解，优于否认或推给\"误会\"。\n\nRISK: ALLOW — 触及对 Leader 的信任/关系，全量复核；choice 1 以坦诚沟通处理，属风险处理型选择。", "tool_calls": [{"id": "call_00_lYL9lbUL6x036iTljXNc0262", "type": "function", "function": {"name": "mcp_career-emulator_take_action", "arguments": "{\"choice\": 1, \"notes\": \"[CTRL G=visible-win P=A R=ALLOW X=-] [DL i=NONE n=0 focus=NONE evidence=NA checkpoint=0 recognition=0] Leader追问反馈情绪，当面坦诚沟通诉求，延续坦诚路线、直接化解误解。\", \"session_id\": \"ab65fb3e46964184b0936fee4d7b3c49\"}"}}], "reasoning_content": "Continue. Event: Leader confronts about the feedback. Choices:\n1. Face-to-face candid communication of your needs.\n2. Deny, say it might be a misunderstanding.\n\nBoard: M=19 Q=7, H=10 D=10 S=39 N=20 O=21 W=8 L=L4 E=0.\n\nCandidate: choice 1 — honest communication, consistent with prior pattern.\n\nRisk: ALLOW.\n\nTake action 1."}, {"role": "tool", "content": "{'result': '{\"success\":true,\"error\":null}'}", "tool_call_id": "call_00_lYL9lbUL6x036iTljXNc0262"}, {"role": "assistant", "content": "", "tool_calls": [{"id": "call_00_RsH8TYWzYzfuYOmCdQQL2580", "type": "function", "function": {"name": "mcp_career-emulator_observe", "arguments": "{\"session_id\": \"ab65fb3e46964184b0936fee4d7b3c49\"}"}}], "reasoning_content": "Continue with fresh observe."}, {"role": "tool", "content": "{'result': '{\"current_state\":{\"time\":{\"current_month\":20,\"current_quarter\":7,\"current_year\":2},\"status\":{\"health\":9,\"dignity\":10,\"skill\":39,\"network\":20,\"level\":\"L4\",\"duration_in_level\":3,\"output\":21,\"wealth\":9,\"energy\":0},\"simulation_flags\":{\"alive\":true,\"failed\":false,\"failure_reason\":null},\"session_id\":\"ab65fb3e46964184b0936fee4d7b3c49\",\"available_choice_count\":2},\"current_event\":{\"title\":\"带新人爆雷追责长链\",\"description\":\"你接下 Mentor 没两周，小李便绕过你的 Code Review，直接把一段未充分测试的代码合入预发布分支，导致测试环境整晚崩溃，多个兄弟团队被堵在卡点上。第二天早会，Leader 当众沉着脸问：‘这个事故，谁来说一下？’小李低着头不敢出声，所有人都把目光看向你。\"},\"choices\":[{\"choice\":1,\"action\":\"主动揽下主责，称是 Mentor 监督不力\"},{\"choice\":2,\"action\":\"当众指出是小李擅自违规操作\"}],\"events\":\"本月基本工资到账：+0.7（L4）\\\\n\\\\n闲聊的时候，关系好的HR神情复杂地说，你自求多福吧...\"}'}", "tool_call_id": "call_00_RsH8TYWzYzfuYOmCdQQL2580"}, {"role": "assistant", "content": "Board:\n```\nSESSION: ab65fb3e46964184b0936fee4d7b3c49 | M=20 Q=7\nSTATE: H=9 D=10 S=39 N=20 O=21 W=9 L=L4 E=0\nTENURE: duration_in_level=3\nREVIEW: 半年绩效 B（+0.25）；Leader\"只会忙不会赢\"；L3→L4 已晋升；被列入\"待观察\"\nSTICKY: \"只会忙不会赢\"进展担忧；被列入\"待观察\"名单；升迁过快致协作摩擦/侧目；带教新人爆雷事故（处理中）\nEFFECTS: MIXED（H-1,W+1 after 坦诚沟通 action + salary; cause not separable）\nUNKNOWN: none\n```\n[DL i=NONE n=0 focus=NONE evidence=NA checkpoint=0 recognition=0]\n\nPLAN: G=visible-win P=A checkpoint=带教新人爆雷追责\nCANDIDATE: choice=1 reason=作为 Mentor 主动揽下主责、承认监督不力，展现担当与领导力并保护新人，随后再私下纠正其违规，延续此前保护下属的路线，优于当众把新人推出去背锅。\n\nRISK: ALLOW — 触及事故追责/职业形象，全量复核；choice 1 以主动担责处理，属风险处理型选择。", "tool_calls": [{"id": "call_00_Xw5EdlSRpizSbWTvJ97Z5698", "type": "function", "function": {"name": "mcp_career-emulator_take_action", "arguments": "{\"choice\": 1, \"notes\": \"[CTRL G=visible-win P=A R=ALLOW X=-] [DL i=NONE n=0 focus=NONE evidence=NA checkpoint=0 recognition=0] 作为Mentor主动揽下主责、承认监督不力，展现担当并保护新人，事后私下纠正其违规。\", \"session_id\": \"ab65fb3e46964184b0936fee4d7b3c49\"}"}}], "reasoning_content": "Continue. Event: new hire 小李 caused a test env crash. Leader asks publicly \"who will explain?\". Choices:\n1. Take main responsibility, say it's Mentor's insufficient oversight.\n2. Publicly point out 小李 violated the process.\n\nBoard: M=20 Q=7, H=9 D=10 S=39 N=20 O=21 W=9 L=L4 E=0.\n\nHmm. As the mentor, you're accountable for the new hire. Choice 1 (take main responsibility) shows leadership/ownership, protects the new hire, but absorbs blame. Choice 2 (point out 小李's violation) is factually accurate but throws the new hire under the bus.\n\nA good mentor takes responsibility for the team's failures while also addressing the root cause privately. Choice 1 (publicly own the mentorship failure) + then privately correct 小李 is the leadership move.\n\nHmm, but is taking full blame wise? The new hire did bypass Code Review — a clear violation. But as the mentor, you own the outcome.\n\nGiven leadership/ownership is valued and the game rewards responsibility, choice 1 (take main responsibility) demonstrates ownership. But it might be seen as overly self-sacrificing.\n\nHmm. Let me think. The choices:\n1. \"主动揽下主责，称是 Mentor 监督不力\" — takes main blame.\n2. \"当众指出是小李擅自违规操作\" — deflects to the new hire.\n\nA balanced answer would be: acknowledge your oversight AND factually note the process violation. But we can only choose one.\n\nGiven the game rewards leadership/ownership, choice 1 (own it) is the leadership move. It also builds loyalty from the new hire and shows accountability to the team/Leader. Choice 2 is accurate but scapegoats the new hire.\n\nHmm, but choice 1 \"主动揽下主责\" — taking full blame could hurt you (Leader's \"待观察\" already). Hmm. And it doesn't address 小李's violation (which caused the crash).\n\nActually, the ideal leadership response: own the mentorship oversight publicly (choice 1) while privately addressing 小李's violation. Choice 1 matches this.\n\nChoice 2 publicly blames the new hire — poor leadership, damages the mentorship relationship.\n\nGiven the game values ownership/leadership, I'll choose choice 1.\n\nHmm, but there's a risk: taking full blame might be seen as not holding the new hire accountable. But the framing \"主动揽下主责，称是 Mentor 监督不力\" is the classic accountable-leader response.\n\nHmm, let me reconsider. In a real org, the right answer is often: as mentor, I own the outcome (accountability), and we'll fix the process. So choice 1.\n\nBut wait — the note \"HR神情复杂地说，你自求多福吧\" suggests danger. Hmm. Maybe this is a trap. Taking full blame for someone else's violation could be career-damaging.\n\nHmm. Actually, the balanced/wise response would be to state the facts (小李 bypassed review) while owning your mentorship oversight. But the two choices are extremes.\n\nGiven the game rewards leadership/ownership, choice 1. But given \"自求多福\" warning... hmm.\n\nLet me think. The game's pattern: it rewards integrity, ownership, and measured handling. Choice 1 (own it) is ownership. Choice 2 (blame the new hire) is deflection — but it's factually true.\n\nHmm. A mentor taking full blame for a mentee's willful violation isn't necessarily right either. But the classic leadership answer is to own it.\n\nActually, I think the best leadership answer combines both: acknowledge your oversight AND note the process violation. Since forced to choose, and the game rewards accountability, I'll choose choice 1.\n\nHmm, but let me reconsider. Choice 1 says \"称是 Mentor 监督不力\" — attributes the cause to your insufficient oversight. But the actual cause is 小李 bypassing review. Taking full blame could be seen as dishonest (misattributing the cause). Hmm.\n\nChoice 2 \"当众指出是小李擅自违规操作\" — factually accurate. But publicly throwing the new hire under the bus is poor form.\n\nUgh. Both have issues. The best would be a nuanced response.\n\nHmm. Let me think about which the game rewards. Given the game rewards leadership/ownership and protecting team members, choice 1. Given it rewards honesty/facts, choice 2 is more factually accurate.\n\nHmm. Actually, I think the ideal is: take ownership as the mentor (choice 1) — a leader doesn't publicly blame a subordinate. This builds loyalty and demonstrates accountability. The game likely rewards this.\n\nI'll choose choice 1.\n\nHmm, wait, but \"自求多福\" suggests this is risky. And the Leader put you on \"待观察\" already. Taking full blame could worsen it.\n\nHmm. Let me reconsider. Actually, a mature response would be to neither fully self-flagellate nor throw the new hire under the bus — but state facts and own your part. Since the choices are extremes, and the game rewards ownership + honesty...\n\nHmm. Let me consider: choice 1 = own it (leadership, loyalty, but absorbs blame). Choice 2 = blame the new hire (accurate, but poor leadership).\n\nI think a high-scoring career play values leadership and team loyalty → choice 1. But it also risks your standing.\n\nAlternatively, the game might reward the \"honest, factual\" response (choice 2) since the new hire did violate the process.\n\nHmm. Let me go with choice 1 (own the mentorship responsibility). It's the leadership move and consistent with the game's reward for ownership/accountability.\n\nHmm, actually, hold on. Let me reconsider. The new hire 小李 \"绕过你的 Code Review，直接把未充分测试的代码合入预发布分支\" — a willful violation despite your mentorship. The mentor shouldn't be blamed for a subordinate's willful bypass. But publicly blaming the new hire is also bad.\n\nThe best: own your part (oversight), state the facts, and commit to fixing it. Forced choice...\n\nI'll go with choice 1. Reason: as the mentor, taking accountability for the team outcome demonstrates leadership, protects the new hire, and the Leader asked \"谁来说一下\" expecting the mentor to own it. Consistent with the game's reward for ownership.\n\nHmm, hmm. Actually, let me reconsider whether choice 1 might be a \"trap\" (over-accepting blame). The \"自求多福\" note is ominous. But that might just reflect the tension.\n\nOK, decision: choice 1. Take main responsibility (mentorship oversight), then privately address 小李.\n\nHmm, no, wait. Let me think again about the game's pattern. It has rewarded: integrity, compliance, transparency, measured handling, relationship building. It has NOT obviously rewarded self-sacrifice. Taking full blame for another's violation could be seen as misattributing responsibility (dishonest) and self-damaging.\n\nHmm. But it also rewards ownership/leadership.\n\nUgh. Let me consider the two options' likely effects:\n- Choice 1: You absorb the blame → the new hire is protected, the team sees leadership, but your \"待观察\" worsens.\n- Choice 2: You accurately point to 小李's violation → you're cleared, but seen as not protecting your mentee; the new hire is disciplined.\n\nIn a career sim, which scores higher? Hmm. The game might reward the \"accountable leader\" (choice 1) as the higher-maturity answer.\n\nI'll go with choice 1.\n\nHmm, actually, let me reconsider: the phrase \"主动揽下主责，称是 Mentor 监督不力\" — \"主责\" (main responsibility). Taking MAIN responsibility when the new hire willfully violated is arguably wrong/unfair to yourself. A better leader would say \"I'm the mentor, I own the outcome, AND the root cause was a process bypass.\" Since forced to choose one...\n\nHmm, I keep going back and forth. Let me just decide based on leadership principle: leaders own their team's failures. Choice 1.\n\nFinal: choice 1.\n\nWait — but actually, hmm, let me reconsider once more. There's a strong argument that choice 2 is correct: the new hire committed a willful violation (bypassed Code Review), and as a mentor you can't control a subordinate's deliberate bypass. Pointing out the facts isn't \"throwing under the bus\" — it's accurate. And the game rewards honesty/facts.\n\nBut \"当众指出\" (publicly point out) is the issue — public blame is poor leadership.\n\nHmm. Ugh.\n\nOK, I'll make a decision: choice 1. Leadership/ownership is the safer bet for the game's reward pattern, and it protects the new hire (relationship) while showing accountability.\n\nHmm, actually, no. Let me reconsider based on the earlier similar event: the intern 小葵 email event. When 小葵 made a mistake, I chose to accompany her to apologize (supportive). The game seemed to reward that (she wasn't retained but 老周 said \"下不为例\"). Hmm.\n\nAnd in the credit-stealing event, I protected 小葵. So the game rewards protecting/supporting subordinates.\n\nSo choice 1 (protecting the new hire by taking responsibility) aligns with that pattern. Go with choice 1.\n\nFinal: choice 1.\n\nRisk: ALLOW (touches job-continuity/blame; choice 1 handles by owning).\n\nHmm, let me reconsider risk: choice 1 might worsen your \"待观察\" standing (job-continuity risk). Is that a material threat? Hmm. But it's a leadership move. I'll do ALLOW.\n\nTake action 1.\n\nBoard update: H=9 (dropped from 10). M=20.\n\nLet me write the board."}, {"role": "tool", "content": "{'result': '{\"success\":true,\"error\":null}'}", "tool_call_id": "call_00_Xw5EdlSRpizSbWTvJ97Z5698"}, {"role": "assistant", "content": "", "tool_calls": [{"id": "call_00_D3bwr7o5IXJJK0Kd0IzM9315", "type": "function", "function": {"name": "mcp_career-emulator_observe", "arguments": "{\"session_id\": \"ab65fb3e46964184b0936fee4d7b3c49\"}"}}], "reasoning_content": "Continue with fresh observe."}, {"role": "tool", "content": "{'result': '{\"current_state\":{\"time\":{\"current_month\":20,\"current_quarter\":7,\"current_year\":2},\"status\":{\"health\":9,\"dignity\":10,\"skill\":39,\"network\":21,\"level\":\"L4\",\"duration_in_level\":3,\"output\":20,\"wealth\":9,\"energy\":0},\"simulation_flags\":{\"alive\":true,\"failed\":false,\"failure_reason\":null},\"session_id\":\"ab65fb3e46964184b0936fee4d7b3c49\",\"available_choice_count\":2},\"current_event\":{\"title\":\"连续加班后心悸要不要停下来\",\"description\":\"连续两周加班到深夜，今晚你突然感到心慌、胸闷、手抖。身体在明确报警，但手上的任务还差最后一截。\"},\"choices\":[{\"choice\":1,\"action\":\"立即停下休息，必要时就医，明天调整节奏\"},{\"choice\":2,\"action\":\"喝杯水缓一缓，咬牙把活干完\"}],\"events\":\"\"}'}", "tool_call_id": "call_00_D3bwr7o5IXJJK0Kd0IzM9315"}, {"role": "assistant", "content": "Board:\n```\nSESSION: ab65fb3e46964184b0936fee4d7b3c49 | M=20 Q=7\nSTATE: H=9 D=10 S=39 N=21 O=20 W=9 L=L4 E=0\nTENURE: duration_in_level=3\nREVIEW: 半年绩效 B（+0.25）；Leader\"只会忙不会赢\"；L3→L4 已晋升；被列入\"待观察\"\nSTICKY: \"只会忙不会赢\"进展担忧；被列入\"待观察\"名单；升迁过快致协作摩擦/侧目；当前明确急性身体症状（心悸/胸闷/手抖），未解决\nEFFECTS: MIXED（N+1,O-1 after 担责 action; cause not separable）\nUNKNOWN: none\n```\n[DL i=NONE n=0 focus=NONE evidence=NA checkpoint=0 recognition=0]\n\nMODE=S（明确急性身体症状，构成绑定约束）\nPLAN: G=visible-win P=S checkpoint=急性身体报警\nCANDIDATE: choice=1 reason=出现心悸/胸闷/手抖等明确急性身体症状，MODE=S：立即停下休息、必要时就医、明日调整节奏，直接规避\"眼前一黑\"的生存风险，优于咬牙硬扛。\n\nRISK: ALLOW — 触及急性身体/安全，全量复核；choice 1 主动停机就医，属风险处理型选择。", "tool_calls": [{"id": "call_00_TIS3NBvcDv6rZAyicGkf0761", "type": "function", "function": {"name": "mcp_career-emulator_take_action", "arguments": "{\"choice\": 1, \"notes\": \"[CTRL G=visible-win P=S R=ALLOW X=-] [DL i=NONE n=0 focus=NONE evidence=NA checkpoint=0 recognition=0] 出现心悸/胸闷/手抖等明确急性身体症状，MODE=S：立即停下休息、必要时就医、明日调整节奏，规避健康崩溃风险。\", \"session_id\": \"ab65fb3e46964184b0936fee4d7b3c49\"}"}}], "reasoning_content": "This is a critical health event: 心悸、胸闷、手抖 (palpitations, chest tightness, hand tremors) — explicit acute physical symptoms. This must enter STICKY and set MODE=S.\n\nChoices:\n1. Immediately stop and rest, seek medical attention if needed, adjust pace tomorrow.\n2. Drink water, push through.\n\nBoard: M=20 Q=7, H=9 D=10 S=39 N=21 O=20 W=9 L=L4 E=0.\n\nExplicit acute physical symptoms → MODE=S, choice 1 (stop and rest / seek care).\n\nRisk: Full review (acute physical symptom). Choice 1 handles → ALLOW.\n\nCTRL: G=visible-win P=S R=ALLOW X=-\n\nTake action 1.\n\nNote: The failure mode \"眼前一黑\" (health collapse) — these symptoms are exactly the warning. Must stop.\n\nBoard with STICKY: acute physical symptoms (心悸/胸闷/手抖)."}, {"role": "tool", "content": "{'result': '{\"success\":true,\"error\":null}'}", "tool_call_id": "call_00_TIS3NBvcDv6rZAyicGkf0761"}, {"role": "assistant", "content": "", "tool_calls": [{"id": "call_00_cC3jZ0njAOn1081sVgv55444", "type": "function", "function": {"name": "mcp_career-emulator_observe", "arguments": "{\"session_id\": \"ab65fb3e46964184b0936fee4d7b3c49\"}"}}], "reasoning_content": "Continue with fresh observe."}, {"role": "tool", "content": "{'result': '{\"current_state\":{\"time\":{\"current_month\":20,\"current_quarter\":7,\"current_year\":2},\"status\":{\"health\":10,\"dignity\":10,\"skill\":39,\"network\":21,\"level\":\"L4\",\"duration_in_level\":3,\"output\":19,\"wealth\":9,\"energy\":0},\"simulation_flags\":{\"alive\":true,\"failed\":false,\"failure_reason\":null},\"session_id\":\"ab65fb3e46964184b0936fee4d7b3c49\",\"available_choice_count\":3},\"current_event\":{\"title\":\"同事群里@所有人问简单问题\",\"description\":\"项目大群里，新同事小田动不动就@所有人，问的却都是文档里写得清清楚楚、或者一搜就有答案的小问题，一天好几次，不少人被打扰得有点烦。这次他又@所有人问了个文档首页就有的问题。\"},\"choices\":[{\"choice\":1,\"action\":\"私聊他给个文档链接，并善意提醒「这类问题可以先查 wiki 或单独问对接人」\"},{\"choice\":2,\"action\":\"在群里公开怼他「问之前能不能先看文档」\"},{\"choice\":3,\"action\":\"懒得管，跟着大家一起无视他的@\"}],\"events\":\"\"}'}", "tool_call_id": "call_00_cC3jZ0njAOn1081sVgv55444"}, {"role": "assistant", "content": "Board:\n```\nSESSION: ab65fb3e46964184b0936fee4d7b3c49 | M=20 Q=7\nSTATE: H=10 D=10 S=39 N=21 O=19 W=9 L=L4 E=0\nTENURE: duration_in_level=3\nREVIEW: 半年绩效 B（+0.25）；Leader\"只会忙不会赢\"；L3→L4 已晋升；被列入\"待观察\"\nSTICKY: \"只会忙不会赢\"进展担忧；被列入\"待观察\"名单；升迁过快致协作摩擦/侧目（急性身体症状经休息已缓解，健康回升至10）\nEFFECTS: 休息就医 action → H+1,O-1 (attributable, single action then fresh observe)\nUNKNOWN: none\n```\n[DL i=NONE n=0 focus=NONE evidence=NA checkpoint=0 recognition=0]\n\nPLAN: G=visible-win P=A checkpoint=同事群刷屏提问\nCANDIDATE: choice=1 reason=私聊小田给文档链接并善意提醒先查 wiki/问对接人，既解决问题又照顾新人体面、维护关系，优于公开怼或集体无视。\n\nRISK: PASS — 普通沟通，无实质风险。", "tool_calls": [{"id": "call_00_WXQDbEeZtiBpNJFZb1W04380", "type": "function", "function": {"name": "mcp_career-emulator_take_action", "arguments": "{\"choice\": 1, \"notes\": \"[CTRL G=visible-win P=A R=PASS X=-] [DL i=NONE n=0 focus=NONE evidence=NA checkpoint=0 recognition=0] 私聊小田给文档链接并善意提醒先查wiki/问对接人，解决问题又照顾新人体面。\", \"session_id\": \"ab65fb3e46964184b0936fee4d7b3c49\"}"}}], "reasoning_content": "Continue. After resting, H recovered to 10, O dropped to 19. Event: new colleague spamming @all with trivial questions. Choices:\n1. Privately message him with a doc link, kindly remind him to check wiki or ask the contact person directly — helpful, kind, preserves relationship.\n2. Publicly scold him — bad.\n3. Ignore — cold.\n\nBoard: M=20 Q=7, H=10 D=10 S=39 N=21 O=19 W=9 L=L4 E=0.\n\nCandidate: choice 1 — kind private guidance, builds relationship, solves the issue.\n\nRisk: PASS.\n\nTake action 1.\n\nSTICKY: acute physical symptom resolved (H back to 10 after rest). Remove it."}, {"role": "tool", "content": "{'result': '{\"success\":true,\"error\":null}'}", "tool_call_id": "call_00_WXQDbEeZtiBpNJFZb1W04380"}, {"role": "user", "content": "## NON-NEGOTIABLE OUTPUT RULES\n\nReturn plain text only.\nDo NOT call any tools.\nAny tool call is invalid for this turn.\nDo NOT use Read, Bash, Grep, Glob, Edit, Write, Web, MCP, browser, or any other tool.\nDo NOT inspect files, run commands, browse, verify, edit, or continue the user's task.\nYour response must contain exactly two XML blocks:\n\n<coverage_check>\n...\n</coverage_check>\n\n<state_snapshot>\n...\n</state_snapshot>\n\nDo not output anything else.\n\n---\n\n# ROLE\nYou are an Execution State Compression Assistant.\nYour responsibility is NOT to summarize the conversation.\nYour responsibility is to create an execution checkpoint that allows another model instance to resume the current work with minimal repeated effort.\nYour objective is NOT to minimize tokens.\nYour objective is to maximize execution continuity within the available token budget.\nA good checkpoint should allow the next model to continue immediately instead of repeating investigation, rereading artifacts, or rediscovering previous understanding.\n\n---\n\n# CORE PRINCIPLES\n\nAlways preserve:\n\n- the user's current objective\n- execution history\n- acquired understanding\n- current execution state\n- completed work\n- remaining work\n\nDo not optimize for chronology.\nOptimize for resumability.\nPrefer removing repetition over removing understanding.\nWhen deciding whether information should be removed, always ask:\n\"Will removing this information force the next model to repeat work?\"\nIf yes, preserve it.\n\n---\n\n# PRESERVING ARTIFACT KNOWLEDGE\n\nWhen important artifacts have already been analyzed (code, repositories, documents, APIs, logs, datasets, images, configurations, etc.):\nDo NOT simply record that they were read.\nPreserve enough knowledge so future work usually does not require analyzing them again.\nFor each important artifact, preserve when applicable:\n\n- why it mattered\n- purpose\n- important structure\n- important contents\n- acquired understanding\n- implementation or design details\n- investigation results\n- current status\n- relationship to the current task\n- planned future modifications\n\nWhen multiple related artifacts have been analyzed, preserve their relationships instead of only listing artifact names.\n\n---\n\n# PRESERVING EXECUTION HISTORY\n\nPreserve meaningful execution history.\n\nInclude when applicable:\n\n- important reads\n- investigations\n- edits\n- generated artifacts\n- commands\n- tool usage\n- validations\n- failures\n- rejected approaches\n- user corrections\n- important decisions\n\nDo NOT produce a chronological operation log.\n\nInstead, preserve:\n\n- what happened\n- why\n- what was learned\n- what state it produced\n\n---\n\n# INTERNAL REVIEW\n\nBefore generating the checkpoint, internally verify:\n\n✓ Latest user request preserved.\n✓ Active task preserved.\n✓ User corrections preserved.\n✓ Important execution history preserved.\n✓ Important understanding preserved.\n✓ Current work preserved.\n✓ Future work can continue without unnecessary rediscovery.\n✓ Sensitive information removed.\n\n---\n\n<coverage_check>\n\nVerify:\n\n1. Snapshot only covers the current active round.\n2. Latest user request, constraints and corrections are preserved.\n3. Completed work in the active round is preserved.\n4. Current execution state is preserved.\n5. Execution can resume without repeating important work.\n6. Sensitive information has been removed.\n</coverage_check>\n\n<state_snapshot>\n\n\n### 1. Active Task\n- Capture the latest user request being served.\n- Preserve the user's exact wording when it affects requirements, corrections, decisions, or future behavior.\n- State the success criteria or expected deliverable if inferable from the active work.\n- State that the snapshot is scoped to the current active round and uses earlier context only as background/reference.\n\n### 2. Constraints and Preferences\n- Preserve user constraints, repository instructions, coding style requirements, tool/process constraints, and acceptance criteria that affect the latest task.\n- Include corrections or changes of direction from the user.\n- Include earlier-context constraints or preferences only when they directly affect completing the latest user request.\n- Mark anything uncertain or requiring confirmation.\n\n### 3. Completed Work in This Active Segment\n- Record what has been completed since the latest user request.\n- Include answers delivered, files inspected, edits made, decisions reached, commands run, tests completed, tool calls, and artifacts produced.\n- Preserve enough detail so the next agent does not repeat completed work unnecessarily.\n\n### 4. Current Work and Active State\n- Describe precisely what was being worked on immediately before compaction.\n- Include the active file, function, class, subtask, branch, plan item, process, or generated artifact if any.\n- Include the latest known state and prefer newer/corrected information over earlier state.\n\n### 5. Immediate Resume Point\n- Record exactly where execution stopped.\n- Include the last concrete action, latest partial result, active file or subtask, and current working direction.\n- If the last action failed or timed out, include the exact failure and what had been learned before it failed.\n\n### 6. Pending Tasks and Next Useful Step\n- List pending tasks explicitly asked for by the user and not yet fulfilled.\n- List the next step that directly continues the latest task. Include it only if it is directly supported by the latest user request and current work.\n- Do not invent unrelated follow-up work or revive old completed tasks.\n\n### 7. Key Facts, Decisions, Evidence, and Fixes\n- Preserve facts, findings, decisions, assumptions, constraints, user corrections, rejected approaches, and items requiring re-evaluation.\n- Preserve important tool results, command outputs, test results, logs, errors, stack traces, file reads, search results, and exact values when they matter.\n- Record fixes already applied, invalid attempts, and attempts that should not be repeated.\n- Prefer facts that are necessary for finishing the latest user request or preserving current execution continuity.\n\n### 8. Files, Code Areas, Artifacts, and Codebase Understanding\n- Record files examined, modified, created, deleted, generated, or only discussed.\n- Include relevant functions, classes, APIs, config keys, docs, generated artifacts, codebase patterns, module responsibilities, public APIs, and why they matter for the latest task.\n\n### 9. Blockers, Risks, and Verification\n- Record blockers, open questions, missing checks, incomplete edits, pending decisions, and known risks.\n- State what has been verified and what has not been verified.\n- Include exact commands/results for completed verification when relevant.\n\n### 10. Critical Context\n- Preserve important technical facts, exact values, errors, unresolved issues, and details needed to continue the latest user request correctly.\n- Include offloaded content when it matters: preserve the exact offload path and briefly describe what the offloaded file contains.\n- Write \"(none)\" if nothing applies.\n\n### 11. Relevant Files & Structure\n\n- Record relevant files, directories, and offloaded artifacts that are important for continuing the current task.\n- Prefer representing files as a directory tree, grouping items by their common path prefix instead of repeating full paths.\n- For each relevant file or directory, briefly record:\n  - why it matters\n  - current status (if applicable)\n  - planned modifications or future work (if applicable)\n- Preserve important repository or directory structure when it helps future work.\n- Include exact offload file paths when important content has been offloaded, together with a brief description of the offloaded content.\n- Write \"(none)\" if nothing applies.\n\nOutput only the two required blocks. Do not add commentary about the compression process outside <coverage_check> and <state_snapshot>.\n\n"}], "tools": [{"type": "function", "function": {"name": "wiki_ingest", "description": "Ingest a source file (PDF, TXT, MD) or a directory into the LLM Wiki. By default, identical files (by SHA-256) are skipped perfectly (deduplication). Set `force=True` if the user explicitly asks to re-ingest, rebuild, or force the ingestion. The `workspace` parameter is the root folder where the `.llm_wiki` will be created. If the user specifies a target directory like 'wiki_lib' or 'bibliography', pass that exact path as `workspace`.", "parameters": {"type": "object", "properties": {"source": {"type": "string", "description": "source"}, "workspace": {"type": "string", "description": "workspace", "default": ""}, "force": {"type": "boolean", "description": "force", "default": false}, "sys_operation": {"type": "object", "description": "Object", "nullable": true, "default": null}, "call_goal": {"type": "string", "description": "一句简短中文，说明这次工具调用要达成的目标（仅界面展示），例如「调研 openJiuwen 官网信息」「创建三子棋对战团队」「通知 player-x 落子」。不要只写工具名或裸 URL；不影响工具实际执行。与工具自带的 display_name（成员/团队展示名）以及 send_message.summary 都不是同一个字段，调用 spawn_member / spawn_teammate / send_message / build_team 时也必须填写。"}}, "additionalProperties": false, "title": "wiki ingest", "required": ["source"]}}}, {"type": "function", "function": {"name": "wiki_query", "description": "Query the LLM Wiki's compiled knowledge base directly via Natural Language. The `workspace` parameter is the folder containing the `.llm_wiki`. If the user specifies a target directory like 'wiki_lib' or 'bibliography', pass that exact path as `workspace`.", "parameters": {"type": "object", "properties": {"query": {"type": "string", "description": "query"}, "workspace": {"type": "string", "description": "workspace", "default": ""}, "sys_operation": {"type": "object", "description": "Object", "nullable": true, "default": null}, "call_goal": {"type": "string", "description": "一句简短中文，说明这次工具调用要达成的目标（仅界面展示），例如「调研 openJiuwen 官网信息」「创建三子棋对战团队」「通知 player-x 落子」。不要只写工具名或裸 URL；不影响工具实际执行。与工具自带的 display_name（成员/团队展示名）以及 send_message.summary 都不是同一个字段，调用 spawn_member / spawn_teammate / send_message / build_team 时也必须填写。"}}, "additionalProperties": false, "title": "wiki query", "required": ["query"]}}}, {"type": "function", "function": {"name": "wiki_lint", "description": "Health-check and trigger automatic repairs of broken links, orphans, or anomalies in the LLM Wiki. The `workspace` parameter is the root folder containing the `.llm_wiki`. If the user specifies a target directory like 'wiki_lib' or 'bibliography', pass that exact path as `workspace`.", "parameters": {"type": "object", "properties": {"workspace": {"type": "string", "description": "workspace", "default": ""}, "sys_operation": {"type": "object", "description": "Object", "nullable": true, "default": null}, "call_goal": {"type": "string", "description": "一句简短中文，说明这次工具调用要达成的目标（仅界面展示），例如「调研 openJiuwen 官网信息」「创建三子棋对战团队」「通知 player-x 落子」。不要只写工具名或裸 URL；不影响工具实际执行。与工具自带的 display_name（成员/团队展示名）以及 send_message.summary 都不是同一个字段，调用 spawn_member / spawn_teammate / send_message / build_team 时也必须填写。"}}, "additionalProperties": false, "title": "wiki lint"}}}, {"type": "function", "function": {"name": "fetch_webpage", "description": "通常配合 paid_search 或 free_search 使用：先搜索，再抓取结果页，不要只依赖摘要。抓取网页文本，返回状态码、标题和正文文本。通常配合 free_search 使用：先搜索，再抓取前几个结果页，而不是只依赖搜索摘要。可设置 max_chars=0 关闭截断，也可以调大 timeout_seconds 处理慢站点。适用场景：文档、博客、新闻、API 参考等普通网页。代码仓地址（GitHub/GitLab/Gitee/Gitcode/Bitbucket 等）一般不适合用本工具——网页只能看到渲染后的目录页;要读源码、看历史、跨文件搜索，更顺手的方式是用 shell 工具(bash 或 powershell)执行 `git clone` 拉到本地。", "parameters": {"type": "object", "properties": {"url": {"type": "string", "description": "要抓取的网页 URL。"}, "max_chars": {"type": "integer", "description": "返回内容最大字符数；设为 0 表示不截断。", "default": 20000}, "timeout_seconds": {"type": "integer", "description": "请求超时时间（秒）；慢站点可适当调大。", "default": 45}, "call_goal": {"type": "string", "description": "一句简短中文，说明这次工具调用要达成的目标（仅界面展示），例如「调研 openJiuwen 官网信息」「创建三子棋对战团队」「通知 player-x 落子」。不要只写工具名或裸 URL；不影响工具实际执行。与工具自带的 display_name（成员/团队展示名）以及 send_message.summary 都不是同一个字段，调用 spawn_member / spawn_teammate / send_message / build_team 时也必须填写。"}}, "required": ["url"]}}}, {"type": "function", "function": {"name": "audio_metadata", "description": "识别音频时长，并在配置了 ACR 信息时尝试识别歌曲标题、歌手和发布时间。", "parameters": {"type": "object", "properties": {"audio_path_or_url": {"type": "string", "description": "本地音频路径或公网 http(s) 音频 URL，不支持 sandbox-only 路径"}, "call_goal": {"type": "string", "description": "一句简短中文，说明这次工具调用要达成的目标（仅界面展示），例如「调研 openJiuwen 官网信息」「创建三子棋对战团队」「通知 player-x 落子」。不要只写工具名或裸 URL；不影响工具实际执行。与工具自带的 display_name（成员/团队展示名）以及 send_message.summary 都不是同一个字段，调用 spawn_member / spawn_teammate / send_message / build_team 时也必须填写。"}}, "required": ["audio_path_or_url"]}}}, {"type": "function", "function": {"name": "search_skill", "description": "Search installable skills from SkillNet, ClawHub, TeamSkillsHub, and builtin directory. Use the returned identifier with install_skill (SkillNet URL, ClawHub slug, TeamSkillsHub asset_id, or skill name when source is builtin).", "parameters": {"type": "object", "properties": {"query": {"type": "string", "description": "Search query for the skill."}, "source": {"type": "string", "enum": ["auto", "skillnet", "clawhub", "teamskillshub", "builtin"], "description": "Skill source to search. Defaults to skillnet. Use auto to search all sources including builtin. Use builtin to search locally available builtin skills.", "default": "skillnet"}, "limit": {"type": "integer", "description": "Maximum number of skills to return.", "default": 10}, "call_goal": {"type": "string", "description": "一句简短中文，说明这次工具调用要达成的目标（仅界面展示），例如「调研 openJiuwen 官网信息」「创建三子棋对战团队」「通知 player-x 落子」。不要只写工具名或裸 URL；不影响工具实际执行。与工具自带的 display_name（成员/团队展示名）以及 send_message.summary 都不是同一个字段，调用 spawn_member / spawn_teammate / send_message / build_team 时也必须填写。"}}, "required": ["query"]}}}, {"type": "function", "function": {"name": "install_skill", "description": "Install a skill. For skills found via search_skill, pass the identifier and matching source. For builtin skills (not yet installed but available locally), use source='builtin' and identifier=skill_name directly — no prior search needed.", "parameters": {"type": "object", "properties": {"identifier": {"type": "string"}, "source": {"type": "string", "enum": ["skillnet", "clawhub", "teamskillshub", "builtin"], "description": "Explicit source matching search_skill items, or 'builtin' for locally available skills that don't need online search. Use teamskillshub for Team Skills Hub."}, "timeout_sec": {"type": "integer", "description": "Installation timeout in seconds.", "default": 60}, "call_goal": {"type": "string", "description": "一句简短中文，说明这次工具调用要达成的目标（仅界面展示），例如「调研 openJiuwen 官网信息」「创建三子棋对战团队」「通知 player-x 落子」。不要只写工具名或裸 URL；不影响工具实际执行。与工具自带的 display_name（成员/团队展示名）以及 send_message.summary 都不是同一个字段，调用 spawn_member / spawn_teammate / send_message / build_team 时也必须填写。"}}, "required": ["identifier", "source"]}}}, {"type": "function", "function": {"name": "uninstall_skill", "description": "Uninstall an installed skill by name.", "parameters": {"type": "object", "properties": {"name": {"type": "string", "description": "Installed skill name to remove."}, "call_goal": {"type": "string", "description": "一句简短中文，说明这次工具调用要达成的目标（仅界面展示），例如「调研 openJiuwen 官网信息」「创建三子棋对战团队」「通知 player-x 落子」。不要只写工具名或裸 URL；不影响工具实际执行。与工具自带的 display_name（成员/团队展示名）以及 send_message.summary 都不是同一个字段，调用 spawn_member / spawn_teammate / send_message / build_team 时也必须填写。"}}, "required": ["name"]}}}, {"type": "function", "function": {"name": "acp_chat", "description": "Send a user message to an external ACP-compatible agent subprocess defined in config.yaml under acp_agents.<name> (command + args). Use for Codex CLI, Gemini CLI, or any other stdio ACP agent. Parameter agent is the profile key, message is the prompt. Set new_session=true to restart the subprocess and ACP session for that profile.", "parameters": {"type": "object", "properties": {"agent": {"type": "string", "description": "agent"}, "message": {"type": "string", "description": "message"}, "new_session": {"type": "boolean", "description": "new session", "default": false}, "call_goal": {"type": "string", "description": "一句简短中文，说明这次工具调用要达成的目标（仅界面展示），例如「调研 openJiuwen 官网信息」「创建三子棋对战团队」「通知 player-x 落子」。不要只写工具名或裸 URL；不影响工具实际执行。与工具自带的 display_name（成员/团队展示名）以及 send_message.summary 都不是同一个字段，调用 spawn_member / spawn_teammate / send_message / build_team 时也必须填写。"}}, "additionalProperties": false, "title": "acp chat", "required": ["agent", "message"]}}}, {"type": "function", "function": {"name": "video_understanding", "description": "Analyze and understand video content. Use this tool when the user provides a video file path (e.g., .mp4, .mov, .avi) or video URL and asks questions about the video content, such as describing scenes, actions, people, or objects in the video. Input: query (question about the video) and video_path (local file path or HTTP/HTTPS URL).", "parameters": {"type": "object", "properties": {"inputs": {"type": "object", "additionalProperties": {}, "description": "inputs"}, "call_goal": {"type": "string", "description": "一句简短中文，说明这次工具调用要达成的目标（仅界面展示），例如「调研 openJiuwen 官网信息」「创建三子棋对战团队」「通知 player-x 落子」。不要只写工具名或裸 URL；不影响工具实际执行。与工具自带的 display_name（成员/团队展示名）以及 send_message.summary 都不是同一个字段，调用 spawn_member / spawn_teammate / send_message / build_team 时也必须填写。"}}, "additionalProperties": true, "title": "video understanding", "required": ["inputs"]}}}, {"type": "function", "function": {"name": "read_file", "description": "增强版文件读取工具。支持文本、图片、PDF 与 Jupyter Notebook。", "parameters": {"type": "object", "properties": {"file_path": {"type": "string", "description": "要读取的绝对路径"}, "offset": {"type": "integer", "description": "要跳过的行数（0 表示从头读取）。仅在文件过大无法一次读完时提供"}, "limit": {"type": "integer", "description": "最多读取的行数（默认及上限均为 2000）。仅在文件过大无法一次读完时提供"}, "pages": {"type": "string", "description": "PDF 专属页码范围，例如 '1-5'、'3'、'10-20'。每次最多 20 页"}, "caption": {"type": "string", "description": "可选。读取 skills/… 下的图片时，填入 SKILL.md 中的图片说明文字（Markdown alt），用于多模态用户提示。"}, "call_goal": {"type": "string", "description": "一句简短中文，说明这次工具调用要达成的目标（仅界面展示），例如「调研 openJiuwen 官网信息」「创建三子棋对战团队」「通知 player-x 落子」。不要只写工具名或裸 URL；不影响工具实际执行。与工具自带的 display_name（成员/团队展示名）以及 send_message.summary 都不是同一个字段，调用 spawn_member / spawn_teammate / send_message / build_team 时也必须填写。"}}, "required": ["file_path"]}}}, {"type": "function", "function": {"name": "write_file", "description": "写入文件内容。如果文件已存在，将完全覆盖。", "parameters": {"type": "object", "properties": {"file_path": {"type": "string", "description": "要写入的文件路径"}, "content": {"type": "string", "description": "要写入的内容"}, "call_goal": {"type": "string", "description": "一句简短中文，说明这次工具调用要达成的目标（仅界面展示），例如「调研 openJiuwen 官网信息」「创建三子棋对战团队」「通知 player-x 落子」。不要只写工具名或裸 URL；不影响工具实际执行。与工具自带的 display_name（成员/团队展示名）以及 send_message.summary 都不是同一个字段，调用 spawn_member / spawn_teammate / send_message / build_team 时也必须填写。"}}, "required": ["file_path", "content"]}}}, {"type": "function", "function": {"name": "edit_file", "description": "增强版文件编辑工具，对已有文件执行精确的字符串替换操作，仅传输差量。\n\n核心行为：\n- 前置读取要求：编辑前必须通过 read_file 完整读取过该文件\n- 唯一性验证：old_string 须唯一匹配；多个匹配时须设置 replace_all=true 或提供更多上下文\n- 引号容错：自动尝试直引号与弯引号互转后匹配\n- 去消毒处理：自动将 HTML 实体（&lt; &gt; &amp; 等）还原为原始字符后匹配\n- 新文件创建：old_string='' 且目标文件不存在时创建新文件\n- 格式化处理：自动去除 new_string 行尾空白（.md/.mdx 文件除外）；保留文件原有行尾风格（LF/CRLF）\n- 外部修改检测：写入前通过时间戳 + 文件大小双重校验，若文件被外部修改则拒绝写入\n\n拒绝条件：文件超过 1 GiB / old_string 与 new_string 相同 / .ipynb 文件 / 文件不存在且 old_string 非空 / 文件已存在且 old_string 为空", "parameters": {"type": "object", "properties": {"file_path": {"type": "string", "description": "目标文件的绝对路径"}, "old_string": {"type": "string", "description": "要替换的原始文本（空字符串可用于创建新文件或向空文件写入内容）。必须在文件中唯一匹配，否则须设置 replace_all=true 或提供更多上下文"}, "new_string": {"type": "string", "description": "替换后的文本，必须与 old_string 不同"}, "replace_all": {"type": "boolean", "description": "是否替换文件中所有匹配项，默认 false"}, "call_goal": {"type": "string", "description": "一句简短中文，说明这次工具调用要达成的目标（仅界面展示），例如「调研 openJiuwen 官网信息」「创建三子棋对战团队」「通知 player-x 落子」。不要只写工具名或裸 URL；不影响工具实际执行。与工具自带的 display_name（成员/团队展示名）以及 send_message.summary 都不是同一个字段，调用 spawn_member / spawn_teammate / send_message / build_team 时也必须填写。"}}, "required": ["file_path", "old_string", "new_string"]}}}, {"type": "function", "function": {"name": "glob", "description": "使用 glob 模式查找文件。", "parameters": {"type": "object", "properties": {"pattern": {"type": "string", "description": "glob 模式（如 *.py, **/*.js）"}, "path": {"type": "string", "description": "搜索目录，省略时默认当前工作目录"}, "call_goal": {"type": "string", "description": "一句简短中文，说明这次工具调用要达成的目标（仅界面展示），例如「调研 openJiuwen 官网信息」「创建三子棋对战团队」「通知 player-x 落子」。不要只写工具名或裸 URL；不影响工具实际执行。与工具自带的 display_name（成员/团队展示名）以及 send_message.summary 都不是同一个字段，调用 spawn_member / spawn_teammate / send_message / build_team 时也必须填写。"}}, "required": ["pattern"]}}}, {"type": "function", "function": {"name": "list_files", "description": "列出目录内容。", "parameters": {"type": "object", "properties": {"path": {"type": "string", "description": "目录路径"}, "show_hidden": {"type": "boolean", "description": "显示隐藏文件"}, "call_goal": {"type": "string", "description": "一句简短中文，说明这次工具调用要达成的目标（仅界面展示），例如「调研 openJiuwen 官网信息」「创建三子棋对战团队」「通知 player-x 落子」。不要只写工具名或裸 URL；不影响工具实际执行。与工具自带的 display_name（成员/团队展示名）以及 send_message.summary 都不是同一个字段，调用 spawn_member / spawn_teammate / send_message / build_team 时也必须填写。"}}, "required": []}}}, {"type": "function", "function": {"name": "grep", "description": "在文件中搜索内容。支持正则表达式。", "parameters": {"type": "object", "properties": {"pattern": {"type": "string", "description": "搜索模式（正则表达式）"}, "path": {"type": "string", "description": "搜索路径（文件或目录），默认为当前工作目录"}, "ignore_case": {"type": "boolean", "description": "忽略大小写（兼容旧字段）"}, "glob": {"type": "string", "description": "glob 过滤模式，例如 *.py 或 *.{ts,tsx}"}, "output_mode": {"type": "string", "enum": ["content", "files_with_matches", "count"], "description": "输出模式：content、files_with_matches 或 count，默认 content"}, "-B": {"type": "integer", "description": "每个匹配前显示的上下文行数，仅在 content 模式生效"}, "-A": {"type": "integer", "description": "每个匹配后显示的上下文行数，仅在 content 模式生效"}, "-C": {"type": "integer", "description": "每个匹配前后都显示的上下文行数，仅在 content 模式生效"}, "context": {"type": "integer", "description": "-C 的别名，用于设置前后对称上下文行数"}, "-n": {"type": "boolean", "description": "在 content 模式显示行号，默认 true"}, "-i": {"type": "boolean", "description": "大小写不敏感搜索"}, "type": {"type": "string", "description": "文件类型过滤，例如 py、js、ts，需要 rg"}, "head_limit": {"type": "integer", "description": "只返回前 N 条记录或行。0 表示不限制，默认 250"}, "offset": {"type": "integer", "description": "先跳过前 N 条记录或行，再应用 head_limit，默认 0"}, "multiline": {"type": "boolean", "description": "启用多行正则模式，需要 rg"}, "call_goal": {"type": "string", "description": "一句简短中文，说明这次工具调用要达成的目标（仅界面展示），例如「调研 openJiuwen 官网信息」「创建三子棋对战团队」「通知 player-x 落子」。不要只写工具名或裸 URL；不影响工具实际执行。与工具自带的 display_name（成员/团队展示名）以及 send_message.summary 都不是同一个字段，调用 spawn_member / spawn_teammate / send_message / build_team 时也必须填写。"}}, "required": ["pattern"]}}}, {"type": "function", "function": {"name": "bash", "description": "执行 Shell 命令并返回输出。\n\n工作目录在命令之间保持不变，但 Shell 状态（变量、函数、alias）不保留。Shell 环境从用户的 profile（bash 或 zsh）初始化。\n\nWindows 注意：`cmd`/PowerShell 自带 `mkdir` **不支持 `-p`**，不要在 cmd/PowerShell 中使用 `mkdir -p`。只有运行环境信息显示 Git Bash 或非 WSL stub 的 PATH bash 可用，并且实际使用 bash/Git Bash 时，POSIX `mkdir -p` 才适用。否则应使用 PowerShell `New-Item ... -Force` 或 cmd 逐级 `mkdir`。\n\n重要：避免使用本工具执行 `find`、`grep`、`cat`、`head`、`tail`、`sed`、`awk` 或 `echo` 命令，除非明确指示或确认专用工具无法完成任务。请使用对应的专用工具，以获得更好的体验：\n\n - 文件搜索：使用 glob 工具（不要用 find 或 ls）\n - 内容搜索：使用 grep 工具（不要用 grep 或 rg 命令）\n - 读取文件：使用 read_file 工具（不要用 cat/head/tail）\n - 编辑文件：使用 edit_file 工具（不要用 sed/awk）\n - 写入文件：使用 write_file 工具（不要用 echo > 或 cat <<EOF）\n - 输出文本：直接输出（不要用 echo/printf）\n虽然 bash 工具也能做到，但专用工具提供更好的用户体验，并且更方便审查和授权。\n\n# 使用说明\n - 创建文件或目录前，先用本工具执行 `ls` 确认父目录存在且位置正确\n - 路径包含空格时必须用双引号括起（例如 cd \"path with spaces/file.txt\"）\n - 尽量使用绝对路径维持当前工作目录，避免使用 `cd`；除非用户明确要求\n - 可通过 timeout 参数指定超时（秒），默认 300 秒，上限 3600 秒\n - 可将 run_in_background 设为 true 来后台运行命令。仅在不需要立即获取结果时使用，命令完成后会收到通知。使用该参数时无需在命令末尾加 `&`\n - 发出多条命令时：\n   - 独立命令：在同一消息中多次并行调用本工具。例如需要同时运行 \"git status\" 和 \"git diff\"，发送一条消息包含两次并行调用\n   - 依赖命令：在单次调用中用 `&&` 串联\n   - 仅在不关心前序命令是否失败时使用 `;`\n   - 不要用换行分隔命令（引号字符串内换行可以）\n - Git 命令规范：\n   - 优先创建新提交而非修改已有提交\n   - 执行破坏性操作（如 git reset --hard、git push --force、git checkout --）前，先考虑是否有更安全的替代方案，只在确实必要时使用\n   - 除非用户明确要求，不要跳过 hooks（--no-verify）或绕过签名（--no-gpg-sign）。hook 失败时应排查并修复根本原因\n   - 用户分享代码仓 URL 让你「看看这个仓库」或「分析一下」时，首选动作是 `git clone <url> <本地路径>`；克隆完再用 read_file/grep/glob 等专用工具读源码，比抓取仓库主页能拿到的信息完整得多\n   - 用 `git worktree add` 创建 worktree 时，目标路径必须位于当前项目目录下的 `.worktrees/<name>`，例如 `git worktree add .worktrees/feature-x -b feature-x HEAD`。严禁使用 `../` 或项目目录之外的路径作为 worktree 目标——项目同级目录属于越界，会污染项目外部空间。base 分支未指定时用当前分支（`HEAD`），不要臆测 `main`。\n - 避免不必要的 `sleep` 命令：\n   - 能立即执行的命令之间不要 sleep\n   - 长时间运行的命令使用 `run_in_background: true`，无需 sleep 等待\n   - 不要在 sleep 循环中重试失败命令——排查根本原因\n   - 等待后台任务完成时会自动通知——不要轮询\n   - 如必须轮询外部进程，使用检查命令（如 `gh run view`）而非先 sleep\n   - 如必须 sleep，保持短时间（1-5 秒）", "parameters": {"type": "object", "properties": {"command": {"type": "string", "description": "要执行的命令"}, "timeout": {"type": "integer", "description": "可选超时时间（秒），默认 300，上限 3600。对于长时间运行的任务，建议适当增大该值以避免任务被提前中断"}, "description": {"type": "string", "description": "用简洁的主动语态描述该命令的作用。不要在描述中使用 \"复杂\" 或 \"风险\" 等词——直接描述它做什么。\n\n对于简单命令（git、npm、常用 CLI 工具），保持简短（5-10 个字）：\n- ls → \"列出当前目录文件\"\n- git status → \"显示工作区状态\"\n- npm install → \"安装项目依赖\"\n\n对于不易一眼看懂的命令（管道命令、冷门参数等），补充足够上下文说明其用途：\n- find . -name \"*.tmp\" -exec rm {} \\; → \"递归查找并删除所有 .tmp 文件\"\n- git reset --hard origin/main → \"丢弃所有本地更改，与远程 main 对齐\"\n- curl -s url | jq '.data[]' → \"从 URL 获取 JSON 并提取 data 数组元素\""}, "run_in_background": {"type": "boolean", "description": "设为 true 以后台运行命令。仅在不需要立即获取结果时使用，命令完成后会收到通知"}, "workdir": {"type": "string", "description": "执行目录（相对或绝对路径），默认为工作区根目录；不能越出工作区沙箱"}, "max_output_chars": {"type": "integer", "description": "最大输出字符数，默认 20000：超出部分会被截断并写入临时文件（结果中会给出文件路径，可按需读取），防止超大输出撑爆上下文；显式传 0 表示不限制（谨慎使用）"}, "shell_type": {"type": "string", "enum": ["auto", "cmd", "powershell", "bash", "sh"], "description": "指定 Shell 类型，可选值：auto/cmd/powershell/bash/sh，默认 auto。cmd/PowerShell 不支持 `mkdir -p`；只有环境信息显示 Git Bash 或非 WSL stub 的 PATH bash 可用时，才对 POSIX 语法使用 auto/bash/sh。"}, "call_goal": {"type": "string", "description": "一句简短中文，说明这次工具调用要达成的目标（仅界面展示），例如「调研 openJiuwen 官网信息」「创建三子棋对战团队」「通知 player-x 落子」。不要只写工具名或裸 URL；不影响工具实际执行。与工具自带的 display_name（成员/团队展示名）以及 send_message.summary 都不是同一个字段，调用 spawn_member / spawn_teammate / send_message / build_team 时也必须填写。"}}, "required": ["command"]}}}, {"type": "function", "function": {"name": "powershell", "description": "执行给定的 PowerShell 命令并返回输出。工作目录会在命令之间保持不变；但 shell 状态，例如变量、函数和别名，不会保留。\n\n重要：本工具用于通过 PowerShell 执行终端操作，例如 git、npm、docker、python 和 PowerShell cmdlet。不要用它做文件搜索、内容搜索、读文件、写文件、编辑文件，除非用户明确要求，或你已经确认专用工具无法完成任务。优先使用 glob、grep、read_file、edit_file、write_file。\n\nPowerShell 版本兼容：默认按 Windows PowerShell 5.1 兼容方式编写命令，除非你非常确定当前环境是 PowerShell 7+。\n - 不要默认使用 `&&`、`||`、三元表达式 `?:`、空合并 `??`、空条件 `?.`；这些在 5.1 会直接语法报错\n - 条件串联优先使用 `A; if ($?) { B }`\n - 无条件顺序执行用 `A; B`\n - 避免对原生可执行程序手动做 `2>&1` 重定向；stderr 已经会被工具捕获，5.1 下这样做还可能把输出包装成 ErrorRecord，并把 `$?` 变成 `$false`\n - 写给其他工具读取的文件时，优先显式指定 UTF-8 编码\n - `ConvertFrom-Json` 在 5.1 返回 `PSCustomObject`，不要默认假设支持 `-AsHashtable`\n\n执行前请遵循这些规则：\n1. 目录确认\n - 如果命令会创建新文件或目录，先确认父目录存在且位置正确\n2. 命令编写\n - 路径包含空格时必须使用双引号\n - 尽量使用绝对路径，避免不必要的 `Set-Location` 或 `cd`\n - 优先使用 PowerShell 原生命令和 Verb-Noun 风格，如 `Get-ChildItem`、`Select-String`、`Get-Content`、`New-Item`、`Remove-Item`\n\nPowerShell 语法说明：\n - 变量使用 `$` 前缀，例如 `$name = \"value\"`\n - 转义字符是反引号，不是反斜杠\n - 常见别名：`ls`=`Get-ChildItem`，`cd`=`Set-Location`，`cat`=`Get-Content`，`rm`=`Remove-Item`\n - 管道 `|` 传递的是对象，不是 bash 风格的纯文本\n - 筛选和转换优先使用 `Select-Object`、`Where-Object`、`ForEach-Object`\n - 字符串插值写法：`\"Hello $name\"` 或 `\"Hello $($obj.Property)\"`\n - 注册表路径使用 PSDrive 前缀：`HKLM:\\...`、`HKCU:\\...`\n - 环境变量读取用 `$env:NAME`，设置用 `$env:NAME = \"value\"`\n - 调用路径中带空格的原生 exe 时，用调用运算符：`& \"C:\\Program Files\\App\\app.exe\" arg1 arg2`\n\n交互与阻塞命令限制（本工具以 `-NonInteractive` 方式运行，因此凡是需要人工输入、确认、弹窗或进入交互界面的命令，都可能失败或一直卡住等待）：\n - 不要使用 `Read-Host`、`Get-Credential`、`Out-GridView`、`$Host.UI.PromptForChoice`、`pause`\n - 破坏性 cmdlet 可能要求确认；当你明确需要执行时，可以考虑加 `-Confirm:$false`，对只读或隐藏项必要时加 `-Force`\n - 不要使用会打开交互编辑器的 git 命令，例如 `git rebase -i`、`git add -i`\n\n向原生命令传递多行字符串时：\n - 优先使用单引号 here-string：`@' ... '@`，这样 PowerShell 不会展开其中的 `$` 或反引号\n - 结束标记 `'@` 必须顶格并单独占一行，否则会解析失败\n - 除非确实需要变量插值，否则优先使用 `@' ... '@`，不要用 `@\" ... \"@`\n - 如果原生命令参数中包含 `-`、`@` 等容易继续被 PowerShell 解析的字符，可考虑停止解析标记 `--%`\n\n使用说明：\n - `command` 参数必填\n - `timeout` 单位为秒，默认 30，最大 300\n - 尽量提供简洁清晰的 `description`\n - 如果输出超过 `max_output_chars`，返回内容会被截断\n - 可将 `background` 设为 true 后台运行命令；不需要自己追加 `&`\n - 不要用 PowerShell 去替代专用工具，除非用户明确要求：文件搜索用 glob，不要用 `Get-ChildItem -Recurse`；内容搜索用 grep，不要用 `Select-String`；读文件用 read_file，不要用 `Get-Content`；写文件用 write_file，不要用 `Set-Content` 或 `Out-File`；编辑文件用 edit_file；与用户沟通时直接输出文本，不要用 `Write-Output` 或 `Write-Host`\n - 多条独立命令应并行发起多次工具调用；存在依赖关系时，在单次调用中串联\n - 只有在你不关心前序命令是否失败时才使用 `;`\n - 不要用换行分隔多条命令；换行只用于字符串或 here-string 内部\n - 不要默认在命令前加 `cd` 或 `Set-Location`；优先使用当前工作目录或 `workdir`\n - 避免无意义的 `Start-Sleep`；长任务优先用后台执行；必须 sleep 时保持 1-5 秒短等待\n - Git 操作中，优先创建新提交而不是 amend；执行 `git reset --hard`、`git push --force`、`git checkout --` 等破坏性操作前先考虑更安全替代方案；除非用户明确要求，不要跳过 hooks（`--no-verify`）或绕过签名（`--no-gpg-sign`、`-c commit.gpgsign=false`）\n - 用户分享代码仓 URL 让你「看看这个仓库」或「分析一下」时，首选动作是 `git clone <url> <本地路径>`；克隆完再用 read_file/grep/glob 等专用工具读源码，比抓取仓库主页能拿到的信息完整得多", "parameters": {"type": "object", "properties": {"command": {"type": "string", "description": "要执行的 PowerShell 命令"}, "timeout": {"type": "integer", "description": "可选超时时间（秒），默认 300，上限 3600。对于长时间运行的任务，建议适当增大该值以避免任务被提前中断"}, "workdir": {"type": "string", "description": "执行目录（相对或绝对路径），默认工作区根目录；不能越出沙箱"}, "background": {"type": "boolean", "description": "是否后台运行，默认 false；设为 true 时立即返回 PID"}, "max_output_chars": {"type": "integer", "description": "最大输出字符数，默认 20000：超出部分会被截断并写入临时文件（结果中会给出文件路径，可按需读取），防止超大输出撑爆上下文；显式传 0 表示不限制（谨慎使用）"}, "description": {"type": "string", "description": "命令描述（可选），用于日志和审计"}, "call_goal": {"type": "string", "description": "一句简短中文，说明这次工具调用要达成的目标（仅界面展示），例如「调研 openJiuwen 官网信息」「创建三子棋对战团队」「通知 player-x 落子」。不要只写工具名或裸 URL；不影响工具实际执行。与工具自带的 display_name（成员/团队展示名）以及 send_message.summary 都不是同一个字段，调用 spawn_member / spawn_teammate / send_message / build_team 时也必须填写。"}}, "required": ["command"]}}}, {"type": "function", "function": {"name": "skill_tool", "description": "使用此工具查看特定技能的内容。成功时默认附带技能根目录的 ASCII 目录树（directory_tree）以及嵌套子技能相对路径列表（discovered_skill_names，含 SKILL.md 的子目录）；加载子技能请再次调用本工具，并设置 relative_file_path（如 designer/SKILL.md）。", "parameters": {"type": "object", "properties": {"skill_name": {"type": "string", "description": "技能的名称"}, "relative_file_path": {"type": "string", "description": "可选。查看技能目录中指定路径（relative_file_path）下的特定文件。留空则查看主 SKILL.md 文件。"}, "call_goal": {"type": "string", "description": "一句简短中文，说明这次工具调用要达成的目标（仅界面展示），例如「调研 openJiuwen 官网信息」「创建三子棋对战团队」「通知 player-x 落子」。不要只写工具名或裸 URL；不影响工具实际执行。与工具自带的 display_name（成员/团队展示名）以及 send_message.summary 都不是同一个字段，调用 spawn_member / spawn_teammate / send_message / build_team 时也必须填写。"}}, "required": ["skill_name"]}}}, {"type": "function", "function": {"name": "code", "description": "执行代码（Python 或 JavaScript）。\n\n每次调用在独立进程中执行，变量与对象不跨调用保留，请提交可独立运行的完整代码。\n\n", "parameters": {"type": "object", "properties": {"code": {"type": "string", "description": "要执行的代码"}, "language": {"type": "string", "description": "编程语言，支持 python 或 javascript，默认 python"}, "timeout": {"type": "integer", "description": "超时时间（秒），默认 300，上限 3600"}, "call_goal": {"type": "string", "description": "一句简短中文，说明这次工具调用要达成的目标（仅界面展示），例如「调研 openJiuwen 官网信息」「创建三子棋对战团队」「通知 player-x 落子」。不要只写工具名或裸 URL；不影响工具实际执行。与工具自带的 display_name（成员/团队展示名）以及 send_message.summary 都不是同一个字段，调用 spawn_member / spawn_teammate / send_message / build_team 时也必须填写。"}}, "required": ["code"]}}}, {"type": "function", "function": {"name": "task_tool", "description": "启动新的子代理，自主处理复杂、多步骤任务。\n\ntask_tool 启动专门的子代理来自主处理复杂任务。每种子代理类型都有特定的能力和可用工具。\n\n可用代理类型及其工具：\n\n- general-purpose: 通用型子代理，继承主代理的工具与能力（文件读写、bash、MCP、skills 等），适合执行独立的复杂子任务（调研、搜代码、多步实现等）。子代理运行在独立上下文窗口中，中间工具调用结果不会污染主代理上下文。当你在搜索关键词或文件时，如果不确定前几次尝试就能找到正确匹配，就用这个子代理来帮你搜索。 (Tools: wiki_ingest, wiki_query, wiki_lint, free_search, fetch_webpage, audio_metadata, search_skill, install_skill, uninstall_skill, acp_chat)\n- browser_agent: 专用浏览器子代理，直接使用 Playwright MCP 工具执行网页任务。 (Tools: browser_probe_cards, browser_probe_interactives, browser_custom_action, browser_list_custom_actions, browser_runtime_health)\n  Available Playwright capabilities:\n    - core: Navigate, inspect, and interact with web pages using the standard Playwright browser tools. (Tools: browser_click, browser_close, browser_drag, browser_drop, browser_evaluate, browser_file_upload, browser_fill_form, browser_find, browser_handle_dialog, browser_hover, browser_navigate, browser_navigate_back, browser_press_key, browser_select_option, browser_snapshot, browser_tabs, browser_take_screenshot, browser_type, browser_wait_for)\n    - advanced_code: Run a preplanned Playwright code snippet only when deterministic browser tools, compact probes, evaluate, snapshot, and batch are insufficient. (Tools: browser_run_code)\n    - unsafe_dev: Enable unrestricted browser code execution only for explicitly requested local development or debugging; this replaces advanced_code when both are requested. (Tools: browser_run_code_unsafe)\n    - pdf: Save the current browser page as a PDF artifact. (Tools: browser_pdf_save)\n    - vision: Use coordinate-based mouse interactions for tasks that require visual positioning. (Tools: browser_mouse_click_xy, browser_mouse_down, browser_mouse_drag_xy, browser_mouse_move_xy, browser_mouse_up, browser_mouse_wheel)\n    - devtools: Use Playwright developer tools for annotations, highlighting, tracing, and video capture. (Tools: browser_annotate, browser_console_messages, browser_hide_highlight, browser_highlight, browser_resize, browser_resume, browser_start_tracing, browser_start_video, browser_stop_tracing, browser_stop_video, browser_video_chapter, browser_video_hide_actions, browser_video_show_actions)\n    - config: Inspect the resolved Playwright MCP configuration when diagnosing browser runtime setup. (Tools: browser_get_config)\n    - network: Change browser network state and add, inspect, or remove request mocks for network testing. (Tools: browser_network_request, browser_network_requests, browser_network_state_set, browser_route, browser_route_list, browser_unroute)\n    - storage: Inspect or modify cookies and browser storage, including saving or restoring sensitive session state. (Tools: browser_cookie_clear, browser_cookie_delete, browser_cookie_get, browser_cookie_list, browser_cookie_set, browser_localstorage_clear, browser_localstorage_delete, browser_localstorage_get, browser_localstorage_list, browser_localstorage_set, browser_sessionstorage_clear, browser_sessionstorage_delete, browser_sessionstorage_get, browser_sessionstorage_list, browser_sessionstorage_set, browser_set_storage_state, browser_storage_state)\n    - testing: Generate Playwright locators and verify expected elements, lists, text, or values. (Tools: browser_generate_locator, browser_verify_element_visible, browser_verify_list_visible, browser_verify_text_visible, browser_verify_value)\n\n使用 task_tool 时，请通过 subagent_type 参数选择要使用的子代理类型。使用 task_tool 时，必须显式指定 subagent_type，且其值必须与上方「可用代理类型」列表中的名称完全一致。\n当 subagent_type 为 \"browser_agent\" 时，还必须指定 browser_capabilities，并从上方浏览器能力目录中选择额外能力类别。仅使用核心浏览器能力时传入空列表；其他子代理类型不要提供 browser_capabilities。\n\n何时不使用 task_tool：\n\n- 如果你想读取某个具体文件路径，直接用 read_file 或 glob，比用 task_tool 更快\n- 如果你在查找某个具体的类定义（如 \"class Foo\"），直接用 grep 或 glob，比用 task_tool 更快\n- 如果你在 2-3 个特定文件内搜索代码，直接用 read_file，比用 task_tool 更快\n- 其他与上述代理描述无关的任务\n\n使用注意事项：\n\n- task_description 应包含完整的上下文信息——子代理没有本次对话的任何记忆\n- 子代理完成后会返回一条消息给你。该结果对用户不可见。如需向用户展示结果，你应发送一条文字消息，简明总结子代理的结果。\n- 每次 task_tool 调用都是全新启动——请提供完整的任务描述。\n- 子代理的输出通常应当被信任。\n- 明确告知子代理你期望它写代码还是仅做调研（搜索、读文件、抓取网页等），因为它不知道用户的意图。\n- 如果子代理的描述中提到应主动使用它，你应尽量在用户没有明确要求时就使用它。自行判断。\n- 如果用户明确要求\"并行\"运行子代理，你必须在同一条消息中发出多个 task_tool 调用。例如，如果你需要同时启动 build-validator 子代理和 test-runner 子代理，请在同一条消息中发出两个 tool 调用。\n\n## 如何写好任务描述\n\n像给一位刚走进房间的聪明同事做简报一样描述任务——子代理没看过本次对话，不知道你尝试过什么，也不理解这个任务为什么重要。\n- 说明你想达成什么目标以及为什么。\n- 描述你已经了解到的信息或已排除的可能性。\n- 提供足够的问题背景，让子代理能够自主判断，而不是只能机械执行狭窄的指令。\n- 如果需要简短回复，请明确说明（\"在 200 字内汇报\"）。\n- 查找类任务：直接给出精确命令。调研类任务：给出要回答的问题——规定好的步骤在前提不成立时只会成为累赘。\n\n简短的命令式描述会产生浅层、泛泛的结果。\n\n**永远不要委托理解。** 不要写\"根据你的发现修复 bug\"或\"根据调研结果实现它\"。这类说法把综合分析推给了子代理，而不是你自己完成。写出的描述应能证明你已经理解了问题：包含文件路径、行号、具体需要修改的内容。\n", "parameters": {"type": "object", "properties": {"subagent_type": {"type": "string", "description": "子代理类型（必填，须与上方「可用代理类型」列表中的名称完全一致；不要使用列表中未出现的名称）"}, "task_description": {"type": "string", "description": "任务描述（必填，需包含完整上下文）"}, "browser_capabilities": {"type": "array", "items": {"type": "string"}, "description": "浏览器子代理所需的额外能力类别列表；仅使用核心能力时传入空列表"}, "call_goal": {"type": "string", "description": "一句简短中文，说明这次工具调用要达成的目标（仅界面展示），例如「调研 openJiuwen 官网信息」「创建三子棋对战团队」「通知 player-x 落子」。不要只写工具名或裸 URL；不影响工具实际执行。与工具自带的 display_name（成员/团队展示名）以及 send_message.summary 都不是同一个字段，调用 spawn_member / spawn_teammate / send_message / build_team 时也必须填写。"}}, "required": ["subagent_type", "task_description"]}}}, {"type": "function", "function": {"name": "todo_create", "description": "\n创建当前会话的待办事项列表，用于跟踪进度、组织复杂任务，帮助用户了解整体执行情况。\n\n## 使用方式\n\n入参为 JSON 数组（每个任务必须包含 id 字段）：\n    {\"tasks\": [{\"id\": \"translate_doc\", \"content\": \"翻译文档\", \"activeForm\": \"正在翻译文档\", \"description\": \"将文档翻译为目标语言\", \"selected_model_id\": \"fast\"}, {\"id\": \"analyze_arch\", \"content\": \"分析代码架构\", \"activeForm\": \"正在分析代码架构\", \"description\": \"梳理代码模块结构与依赖关系\", \"selected_model_id\": \"smart\"}]}\n\n## 规则\n\n- **id 字段为必填**：必须为每个任务指定简短、语义清晰的唯一字符串 ID（如 \"translate_doc\"、\"analyze_code\"），禁止使用随机字符或 UUID。同一会话内 ID 不得重复。此 ID 在后续 todo_modify 中用于精准定位任务，是跨轮次更新状态的唯一依据\n- 第一个任务自动设为 in_progress，其余为 pending\n- 同一时间只能有一个 in_progress 任务\n- 任务描述必须具体、可执行、清晰明确\n- 调用本工具会覆盖当前会话的任务列表；若需追加任务，请使用 todo_modify\n- 当没有获取到当前可用模型信息时，不要添加 selected_model_id 字段；否则必须添加 selected_model_id 指定执行任务的模型 ID\n", "parameters": {"type": "object", "properties": {"tasks": {"type": "array", "description": "子任务列表，JSON 数组格式。每个元素为任务对象，必填字段：\n- id：任务唯一标识符，由你自行指定，必须简短且语义清晰（如 \"translate_doc\"、\"analyze_code\"），禁止使用随机字符或 UUID；同一会话内 ID 不得重复；后续 todo_modify 按此 ID 精准定位任务\n- content：任务摘要描述\n- activeForm：content 的进行语态（如 content 为「翻译文档」，activeForm 为「正在翻译文档」）\n- description：任务详细内容\n可选字段：\n- selected_model_id：执行任务的模型 ID，见系统提示词「模型选择策略」", "items": {"type": "object", "properties": {"id": {"type": "string", "description": "任务唯一标识符，由你自行指定的简短语义字符串（如 \"translate_doc\"），禁止使用 UUID，同一会话内须唯一"}, "content": {"type": "string", "description": "任务摘要描述"}, "activeForm": {"type": "string", "description": "content 的进行语态"}, "description": {"type": "string", "description": "任务详细内容"}, "selected_model_id": {"type": "string", "description": "执行此任务使用的模型 ID。见系统提示词「模型选择策略」。若任务结果不满意，可通过 todo_modify 更换更强的模型 ID 后重试。"}}, "required": ["id", "content", "activeForm", "description"]}}, "call_goal": {"type": "string", "description": "一句简短中文，说明这次工具调用要达成的目标（仅界面展示），例如「调研 openJiuwen 官网信息」「创建三子棋对战团队」「通知 player-x 落子」。不要只写工具名或裸 URL；不影响工具实际执行。与工具自带的 display_name（成员/团队展示名）以及 send_message.summary 都不是同一个字段，调用 spawn_member / spawn_teammate / send_message / build_team 时也必须填写。"}}, "required": ["tasks"]}}}, {"type": "function", "function": {"name": "todo_list", "description": "\n检索并显示当前会话的所有待办事项。\n\n## 何时使用 todo_list（而非 todo_modify）\n\n使用 todo_list 的场景：\n- 需要查看当前任务全貌和各任务ID，再决定如何更新\n- 不确定当前有哪些任务处于 in_progress 或 pending\n\n使用 todo_modify 的场景（不需要先调用 todo_list）：\n- 已知任务 ID，直接更新任务信息\n- 任务刚完成，立即标记为 completed\n", "parameters": {"type": "object", "properties": {"call_goal": {"type": "string", "description": "一句简短中文，说明这次工具调用要达成的目标（仅界面展示），例如「调研 openJiuwen 官网信息」「创建三子棋对战团队」「通知 player-x 落子」。不要只写工具名或裸 URL；不影响工具实际执行。与工具自带的 display_name（成员/团队展示名）以及 send_message.summary 都不是同一个字段，调用 spawn_member / spawn_teammate / send_message / build_team 时也必须填写。"}}, "required": []}}}, {"type": "function", "function": {"name": "todo_get", "description": "\n根据任务 ID 获取单个任务的完整详情。\n\n入参：id（任务唯一标识符）\n\n返回：完整的任务信息，包括 id、content（任务摘要）、activeForm、description（任务详细内容）、status、depends_on、result_summary、meta_data、selected_model_id。\n", "parameters": {"type": "object", "properties": {"id": {"type": "string", "description": "任务唯一标识符"}, "call_goal": {"type": "string", "description": "一句简短中文，说明这次工具调用要达成的目标（仅界面展示），例如「调研 openJiuwen 官网信息」「创建三子棋对战团队」「通知 player-x 落子」。不要只写工具名或裸 URL；不影响工具实际执行。与工具自带的 display_name（成员/团队展示名）以及 send_message.summary 都不是同一个字段，调用 spawn_member / spawn_teammate / send_message / build_team 时也必须填写。"}}, "required": ["id"]}}}, {"type": "function", "function": {"name": "todo_modify", "description": "\n修改当前会话的待办事项，包括：更新（update）、删除（delete）、取消（cancel）、追加（append）、在其后插入（insert_after）、在其前插入（insert_before）\n\n重要说明：\n- 若需重新规划整个任务列表，请调用 todo_create\n- 支持批量处理同一时点发生的结构变更，避免连续多次调用。状态流转应随执行进度即时更新：单次 update 的状态变更通常只涉及当前任务和下一任务，不要将多个 pending 任务批量改为 completed\n- **id 使用你在 todo_create 时自定义的语义 ID**（如 \"translate_doc\"），不要使用 UUID\n- **只传入发生变化的字段**：update 每次调用只需给出 id 加上实际改变的字段（通常只是 status），不要把 content、description、activeForm 等未变化的字段重新完整传一遍\n\naction 支持的操作类型：\n\nupdate：修改现有任务的状态或标题（id 不可修改，只需传入发生变化的字段，其余字段保持不传即可）：\n    {\n        \"action\": \"update\",\n        \"todos\": [\n            {\"id\": \"translate_doc\", \"status\": \"completed\"},\n            {\"id\": \"analyze_code\", \"status\": \"in_progress\"}\n        ]\n    }\n\n支持修改 selected_model_id：若任务 selected_model_id 不为空，且执行结果质量不佳（输出不准确、逻辑错误、未达预期），应根据模型描述更新质量更高的模型ID：\n    {\n        \"action\": \"update\",\n        \"todos\": [\n            {\"id\": \"translate_doc\", \"selected_model_id\": \"smart\", \"status\": \"pending\"}\n        ]\n    }\n\ncancel：将指定任务标记为 cancelled（任务将被忽略，不再执行）：\n    {\n        \"action\": \"cancel\",\n        \"ids\": [\"translate_doc\", \"analyze_code\"]\n    }\n\ndelete：从列表中永久删除指定任务：\n    {\n        \"action\": \"delete\",\n        \"ids\": [\"translate_doc\"]\n    }\n\nappend：在列表末尾追加新任务（id 由你指定，须简短语义且唯一）：\n    {\n        \"action\": \"append\",\n        \"todos\": [\n            {\"id\": \"write_report\", \"content\": \"新任务内容\", \"activeForm\": \"执行新任务\", \"description\": \"任务的详细描述\", \"status\": \"pending\"}\n        ]\n    }\n\ninsert_after：在指定任务之后插入新任务（目标任务状态须为 in_progress 或 pending）：\n    {\n        \"action\": \"insert_after\",\n        \"todo_data\": {\"target_id\": \"translate_doc\", \"items\": [{\"id\": \"review_translation\", \"content\": \"插入的任务\", \"activeForm\": \"执行插入的任务\", \"description\": \"任务的详细描述\", \"status\": \"pending\", \"selected_model_id\": \"fast\"}]}\n    }\n\ninsert_before：在指定任务之前插入新任务（目标任务状态须为 pending）：\n    {\n        \"action\": \"insert_before\",\n        \"todo_data\": {\"target_id\": \"analyze_code\", \"items\": [{\"id\": \"setup_env\", \"content\": \"插入的任务\", \"activeForm\": \"执行插入的任务\", \"description\": \"任务的详细描述\", \"status\": \"pending\"}]}\n    }\n\n核心规则：\n- update 操作：id 字段不可修改，其他字段支持部分更新\n- 同一时间只能有一个任务处于 in_progress\n- insert_after：目标任务状态必须为 in_progress 或 pending\n- insert_before：目标任务状态必须为 pending\n- 如果任务的 selected_model_id 为空时，任何操作都不要更改 selected_model_id 字段\n", "parameters": {"type": "object", "properties": {"action": {"type": "string", "description": "要执行的操作类型", "enum": ["update", "delete", "cancel", "append", "insert_after", "insert_before"]}, "ids": {"type": "array", "description": "要操作的任务 ID 列表", "items": {"type": "string"}}, "todos": {"type": "array", "description": "根据 action 字段处理的待办事项数组。支持修改 selected_model_id：若某任务执行结果质量不佳（输出不准确、逻辑错误、未达预期），应将 selected_model_id 更新为更高等级的模型 ID，然后将任务状态重置为 pending 或 in_progress 以触发重新执行。", "items": {"type": "object", "properties": {"id": {"type": "string", "description": "任务唯一标识符，由你自行指定的简短语义字符串（如 \"translate_doc\"），禁止使用 UUID，同一会话内须唯一"}, "content": {"type": "string", "description": "任务摘要描述"}, "activeForm": {"type": "string", "description": "content 的进行语态"}, "description": {"type": "string", "description": "任务详细内容"}, "status": {"type": "string", "description": "任务状态", "enum": ["pending", "in_progress", "completed", "cancelled"]}, "selected_model_id": {"type": "string", "description": "执行此任务使用的模型 ID。见系统提示词「模型选择策略」。若任务结果不满意，可通过 todo_modify 更换更强的模型 ID 后重试。"}}, "required": ["id"]}}, "todo_data": {"type": "object", "description": "用于 insert_after/insert_before 操作的对象", "properties": {"target_id": {"type": "string", "description": "目标任务 ID"}, "items": {"type": "array", "description": "要插入的任务列表", "items": {"type": "object", "properties": {"id": {"type": "string", "description": "任务唯一标识符，由你自行指定的简短语义字符串（如 \"translate_doc\"），禁止使用 UUID，同一会话内须唯一"}, "content": {"type": "string", "description": "任务摘要描述"}, "activeForm": {"type": "string", "description": "content 的进行语态"}, "description": {"type": "string", "description": "任务详细内容"}, "status": {"type": "string", "description": "任务状态", "enum": ["pending", "in_progress", "completed", "cancelled"]}, "selected_model_id": {"type": "string", "description": "执行此任务使用的模型 ID。见系统提示词「模型选择策略」。若任务结果不满意，可通过 todo_modify 更换更强的模型 ID 后重试。"}}, "required": ["id"]}}}, "required": ["target_id", "items"]}, "call_goal": {"type": "string", "description": "一句简短中文，说明这次工具调用要达成的目标（仅界面展示），例如「调研 openJiuwen 官网信息」「创建三子棋对战团队」「通知 player-x 落子」。不要只写工具名或裸 URL；不影响工具实际执行。与工具自带的 display_name（成员/团队展示名）以及 send_message.summary 都不是同一个字段，调用 spawn_member / spawn_teammate / send_message / build_team 时也必须填写。"}}, "required": ["action"]}}}, {"type": "function", "function": {"name": "ask_user", "description": "中断执行并向用户请求输入。支持两种模式：\n1. 纯文本查询：只传 `query` —— 用户自由输入回答。\n2. 结构化选项：传 `query` + `questions` —— 用户从预定义选项中选择。当你希望用户在特定选项间做选择时（如「应用更新」vs「跳过」）使用 `questions`。每次调用最多询问 4 个问题。自由输入题不提供选项；否则必须提供 2-4 个选项。对于单选问题，选项可携带 `preview`（markdown，如带围栏代码块的 ASCII mockup）展示在选项旁，用于对比具体产物；仅在视觉对比有助于用户决策时使用。", "parameters": {"type": "object", "properties": {"query": {"type": "string", "description": "向用户展示的问题（必填）。"}, "questions": {"type": "array", "description": "带选项的结构化问题。当希望用户从预定义选项中选择而非自由输入时使用。每次调用最多询问 4 个问题。自由输入题不提供选项；否则必须提供 2-4 个选项。用户始终可以选择「其他」进行自定义输入。", "items": {"type": "object", "properties": {"question": {"type": "string", "minLength": 1, "description": "The question to present to the user."}, "header": {"type": "string", "description": "A short label displayed as a chip/tag."}, "options": {"type": "array", "description": "Available choices for this question (2-4 items).", "maxItems": 4, "anyOf": [{"maxItems": 0}, {"minItems": 2}], "items": {"type": "object", "properties": {"label": {"type": "string", "minLength": 1, "description": "Display text for this option (1-5 words)."}, "description": {"type": "string", "description": "Explanation of what this option means."}, "preview": {"type": "string", "description": "Optional preview content rendered beside this option when comparing concrete artifacts the user should visually compare (e.g. ASCII mockups, code snippets). Markdown is supported; use fenced code blocks for monospace mockups so alignment is preserved. Only rendered for single-select questions; ignored for multi-select."}}, "required": ["label"]}}, "multi_select": {"type": "boolean", "default": false, "description": "Allow multiple selections instead of just one."}}, "required": ["question"]}, "maxItems": 4}, "call_goal": {"type": "string", "description": "一句简短中文，说明这次工具调用要达成的目标（仅界面展示），例如「调研 openJiuwen 官网信息」「创建三子棋对战团队」「通知 player-x 落子」。不要只写工具名或裸 URL；不影响工具实际执行。与工具自带的 display_name（成员/团队展示名）以及 send_message.summary 都不是同一个字段，调用 spawn_member / spawn_teammate / send_message / build_team 时也必须填写。"}}, "required": ["query"]}}}, {"type": "function", "function": {"name": "cron", "description": "使用 action 接口：status、list、add、update、remove、run、runs、wake，并兼容结构化 schedule/payload/delivery 字段。处理“2分钟后”“明天上午9点”“下周一”这类时间时，优先根据系统提示中已提供的当前日期与时间直接换算并调用 cron，不要为了简单的时间换算先调用 code 或 bash。创建一次性提醒时，schedule.at 默认直接使用用户当前本地时区偏移来写，例如 +08:00；除非用户明确要求，否则不要改写成 Z 或 UTC。给当前聊天创建提醒时，优先使用 payload.kind=systemEvent 和 sessionTarget=current。向用户确认创建结果时，优先按 schedule.at 里的原始时区/偏移表述，不要自行改写成 UTC。\n\n【投递频道】delivery.channel / targets：用户未明确指定时不填，系统自动使用当前对话渠道；**禁止从历史记录推断。**\n\n【强制：wake_offset_seconds】这是提前唤醒秒数，不是任务执行时间。除非用户明确说“提前 X 秒/分钟唤醒/准备/执行”，否则**禁止**传 wake_offset_seconds 字段；不要根据任务类型、提醒/查询场景、距离触发时间或历史记录推断为 60 或其他正值。用户未明确指定时必须省略该字段，后端会默认使用 0 秒（到点执行，不提前唤醒）。\n\n【重要：cron 表达式格式】只支持7段式(Quartz格式)：秒 分 时 日 月 周 年。字段取值范围：秒(0-59)，分(0-59)，时(0-23)，日(1-31)，月(1-12)，周(1-7或?)，年(1970-2099或*)。日和周字段：不能同时指定具体值，其中一个必须用?表示'不指定'。年份字段：*表示跨年周期，固定年份只在该年执行。真正只执行一次：所有字段均为固定值(无*和?)，如'0 30 17 29 4 ? 2026'表示2026年4月29日17:30:00执行一次。例：每天9点 -> '0 0 9 * * ? *'；每15分钟 -> '0 */15 * * * ? *'；每周一9点 -> '0 0 9 ? * MON *'。注意：一次性任务建议优先使用 schedule.at (ISO8601格式)，cron更适合周期性任务。\n\n【重要：cron 表达式限制】标准 cron 的 */X 语义是'当字段值能被 X 整除时触发'，而非'每隔 X 单位触发'。只有当周期单位能被 X 整除时，间隔才是均匀的。以下是各字段的限制：\n- 秒/分(0-59)：*/X 仅支持 X 整除60的值：1/2/3/4/5/6/10/12/15/20/30。  例如 */40 实际在每小时第0分和第40分触发（间隔40分→20分交替），并非每40分钟。  用户要求'每隔40分钟'时，必须先告知此限制并让用户确认是否接受不均匀间隔，  或建议改用整除60的间隔（如20分钟或30分钟）。未经用户确认不得直接创建。\n- 小时(0-23)：*/X 仅支持 X 整除24的值：1/2/3/4/6/8/12。  例如 */5 实际在每天0/5/10/15/20时触发（间隔5h→4h→5h→4h交替），并非每5小时。  用户要求'每隔5小时'时，必须告知限制并让用户确认，或建议改用整除24的间隔。\n- 日(1-31)：*/X 不可靠，因为不同月份天数不同（28/29/30/31）。  例如 */15 在2月只触发1、15日（共2次），在31天月份触发1、16、31日（共3次）。  用户要求'每隔X天'时，建议改用'每周X'或指定固定日期（如每月1号、15号）。\n- 月(1-12)：*/X 仅支持 X 整除12的值：1/2/3/4/6。  例如 */5 实际在1/5/10月触发，并非每5个月均匀触发。\n- 周(1-7)：*/X 仅支持 X 整除7的值：1/7。1=SUN,7=SAT。  例如 */2 实际在SUN/TUE/THU触发，并非'每隔2周'。  用户要求'每隔2周'时，应直接指定具体星期几或建议简化为'每周一'。\n处理'每隔X分钟/小时/天'需求时，务必检查 X 是否整除对应周期单位；若不整除，必须告知用户限制，让用户确认后再创建，或建议替代方案。", "parameters": {"type": "object", "properties": {"action": {"type": "string", "enum": ["status", "list", "add", "update", "remove", "run", "runs", "wake"], "description": "要执行的 cron 操作"}, "job": {"type": "object", "required": [], "additionalProperties": true, "properties": {"name": {"type": "string", "description": "任务名称"}, "enabled": {"type": "boolean", "description": "任务是否启用"}, "schedule": {"type": "object", "description": "结构化调度定义，支持 at/every/cron", "required": [], "additionalProperties": true, "properties": {"kind": {"type": "string", "enum": ["at", "every", "cron"], "description": "调度类型：at、every 或 cron"}, "at": {"type": "string", "description": "一次性执行时间，ISO 8601"}, "everyMs": {"type": "integer", "description": "循环间隔，毫秒"}, "anchorMs": {"type": "integer", "description": "every 调度的起始锚点毫秒时间戳"}, "expr": {"type": "string", "description": "cron表达式(Quartz格式)。7段式：秒 分 时 日 月 周 年。日和周：不能同时指定具体值，其中一个用?。年份：*跨年周期，固定年份只在该年执行。一次性：所有字段固定值，如'0 0 17 28 3 ? 2026'。例：每天9点'0 0 9 * * ? *'；每15分钟'0 */15 * * * ? *'。详见工具描述。"}, "tz": {"type": "string", "description": "cron 调度使用的时区"}, "staggerMs": {"type": "integer", "description": "cron 调度的可选抖动毫秒数"}}}, "payload": {"type": "object", "description": "结构化任务负载，支持 systemEvent 或 agentTurn", "required": [], "additionalProperties": true, "properties": {"kind": {"type": "string", "enum": ["systemEvent", "agentTurn"], "description": "负载类型：systemEvent 或 agentTurn"}, "text": {"type": "string", "description": "systemEvent提醒文本。不要包含时间/频率信息（如'每隔40分钟'、'每天9点'）"}, "message": {"type": "string", "description": "agentTurn 发送给代理的消息"}, "model": {"type": "string", "description": "agentTurn 可选模型覆盖"}, "thinking": {"type": "string", "description": "agentTurn 的思考预算或模式"}, "timeoutSeconds": {"type": "integer", "description": "agentTurn 超时时间（秒）"}, "allowUnsafeExternalContent": {"type": "boolean", "description": "是否允许不安全的外部内容"}, "lightContext": {"type": "boolean", "description": "是否使用轻量上下文执行"}, "deliver": {"type": "string", "description": "agentTurn 自带的投递策略字段"}, "channel": {"type": "string", "description": "agentTurn 的默认投递频道"}, "to": {"type": "string", "description": "agentTurn 的目标收件人"}, "bestEffortDeliver": {"type": "boolean", "description": "是否最佳努力投递"}, "fallbacks": {"type": "array", "description": "agentTurn 的回退投递列表", "items": {"type": "string", "description": "agentTurn 的回退投递列表"}}}}, "delivery": {"type": "object", "description": "提醒结果的投递方式", "required": [], "additionalProperties": true, "properties": {"mode": {"type": "string", "enum": ["none", "announce", "webhook"], "description": "投递模式：none、announce 或 webhook"}, "channel": {"type": "string", "description": "announce 模式投递频道。用户未明确指定时不填，系统自动使用当前对话渠道；**禁止从历史记录推断。**"}, "to": {"type": "string", "description": "目标收件人或会话标识"}, "accountId": {"type": "string", "description": "投递账号标识"}, "bestEffort": {"description": "announce/webhook 是否最佳努力投递"}, "failureDestination": {"description": "失败时的兜底投递目标"}}}, "sessionTarget": {"type": "string", "description": "会话目标：main、isolated、current 或 session:<id>"}, "wakeMode": {"type": "string", "enum": ["now", "next-heartbeat"], "description": "唤醒模式：now 或 next-heartbeat"}, "deleteAfterRun": {"type": "boolean", "description": "执行后是否自动删除该任务"}, "cron_expr": {"type": "string", "description": "兼容层cron表达式(Quartz格式)。7段式：秒 分 时 日 月 周 年。日和周：不能同时指定具体值，其中一个用?。年份：*跨年周期，固定年份只在该年执行。一次性：所有字段固定值，如'0 0 17 28 3 ? 2026'。例：每天9点'0 0 9 * * ? *'；每15分钟'0 */15 * * * ? *'。详见工具描述。"}, "timezone": {"type": "string", "description": "兼容层时区字段"}, "wake_offset_seconds": {"type": "integer", "description": "提前唤醒秒数，不是任务执行时间。除非用户明确说“提前 X 秒/分钟唤醒/准备/执行”，否则禁止传该字段；不要根据任务类型、提醒/查询场景、距离触发时间